achieves_seedPrime\\\\n    (hO : Sheaf.h0 (C.left.moduleKSheaf k) = 1)\\\\n    (h\\\\u03c7 : Sheaf.chi (C.left.moduleKSheaf k) = 1 - (g : \\\\u2124))\\\\n    (p : PrimeSpectrum R_Z)\\\\n    (hne : divUniversalFibreKM C h\\\\u03c0 g r\\\\u2081 r\\\\u2082 b\\\\u2081 i j p.asIdeal.ResidueField \\\\u2260 \\\\u22a5)\\\\n    {z : relCurve C p.asIdeal.ResidueField} (hz : z \\\\u2260 genericPoint (relCurve C p.asIdeal.ResidueField)) :\\\\n    \\\\u2203 x \\\\u2208 (divUniversalFstWindow C \\\\u03c0 h\\\\u03c0 g r\\\\u2081 r\\\\u2082 b\\\\u2081 b\\\\u2082 i j).toSubmodule,\\\\n      relThetaWindowEquiv C R_Z \\\\u03c0 (windowM_choice \\\\u03c0 h\\\\u03c0 g) (relThetaPairH1_windowM C \\\\u03c0 h\\\\u03c0 g) x\\\\n        \\\\u2208 divUniversalSeedK C \\\\u03c0 h\\\\u03c0 g r\\\\u2081 r\\\\u2082 b\\\\u2081 b\\\\u2082 i j \\\\u2227\\\\n      windowCompare R_Z p.asIdeal.ResidueField x \\\\u2260 0 \\\\u2227\\\\n      \\\\u2203 hr : divFamPhi C p.asIdeal.ResidueField \\\\u03c0 (windowM_choice \\\\u03c0 h\\\\u03c0 g) (relThetaPairH1_windowM C \\\\u03c0 h\\\\u03c0 g)\\\\n          (windowCompare R_Z p.asIdeal.ResidueField x) \\\\u2260 0,\\\\n        coeffAt hz ((windowN C p.asIdeal.ResidueField h\\\\u03c0 g\\\\n              - divUniversalSeedFibreDivisor C h\\\\u03c0 g r\\\\u2081 r\\\\u2082 b\\\\u2081 b\\\\u2082 i j hO h\\\\u03c7 p)\\\\n            + Scheme.divOf (relCurve C p.asIdeal.ResidueField \\\\u2198 Spec (CommRingCat.of p.asIdeal.ResidueField))\\\\n                (Units.mk0 (divFamPhi C p.asIdeal.ResidueField \\\\u03c0 (windowM_choice \\\\u03c0 h\\\\u03c0 g) (relThetaPairH1_windowM C \\\\u03c0 h\\\\u03c0 g)\\\\n                    (windowCompare R_Z p.asIdeal.ResidueField x)) hr))\\\\n          = (Scheme.baseDivisorAt p.asIdeal.ResidueField (divUniversalFibreKM C h\\\\u03c0 g r\\\\u2081 r\\\\u2082 b\\\\u2081 i j p.asIdeal.ResidueField)\\\\n              (windowN C p.asIdeal.ResidueField h\\\\u03c0 g - divUniversalSeedFibreDivisor C h\\\\u03c0 g r\\\\u2081 r\\\\u2082 b\\\\u2081 b\\\\u2082 i j hO h\\\\u03c7 p) \\\\u27e8z, hz\\\\u27e9 : \\\\u2124)\\\\n\\\\n=== HOW THE seedUniv REVISION CONSUMES IT (sec z) ===\\\\nsec z := relThetaWindowEquiv C R_Z \\\\u03c0 (windowM_choice \\\\u03c0 h\\\\u03c0 g) (relThetaPairH1_windowM C \\\\u03c0 h\\\\u03c0 g) x, which lies in divUniversalSeedK (2nd component). It is BOTH:\\\\n (a) fibrewise nonzero \\\\u2014 windowCompare R_Z \\\\u03ba(p) x \\\\u2260 0 (3rd component) \\\\u2014 feeds Brick 2 (exists_forall_windowCompare_ne_zero) -> Brick 3 (relPinnedSectionsMap_relThetaResSide_windowEquiv_ne_zero) -> the seed's hfib clause, EXACTLY as the old DivSchemeSeedUnivBridge sec did; AND\\\\n (b) a RELATIVE ACHIEVER at z \\\\u2014 its \\\\u03ba(p)-fibre reading Phi(windowCompare R_Z \\\\u03ba(p) x) cuts EXACTLY d_p: ((N \\\\u2212 d_p) + div reading)_z = baseDivisorAt(divUniversalFibreKM)_z (4th component), i.e. minimal vanishing at z (ord = base-divisor order). z is NOT an extra zero. This is EXACTLY what the old windowCompare\\\\u22600 sec LACKED (I-0288 fact 3); it discharges the I-0288 hle razor AT z.\\\\nSo the revised seedUniv.sec = this x's window image, and the achiever equation is the new content the ann-based h z (brick 3) then extends across D(h z) by excluding the OTHER extra zeros.\\\\n\\\\n=== RESIDUAL (for the seedUniv-revision / brick-3 follow-up) ===\\\\n1. hne (divUniversalFibreKM \\\\u03ba(p) \\\\u2260 \\\\u22a5) is a HYPOTHESIS (matches the DivSchemeSeedUnivBridge seed-prime pattern which took f\\\\u22600). Trivial to discharge: finrank_divUniversalFibreKM_add (AssembleKappa:207) gives finrank + g = h0(O(windowN)); with two_mul_genus_le_deg_windowN + subsingleton_h1_windowN (RR) h0 = degN+1\\\\u2212g \\\\u2265 g+1 > g so finrank \\\\u2265 1, \\\\u2260 \\\\u22a5. The seedUniv revision already produces a nonzero fibre element (RR), so it supplies hne directly. NOT derived here to keep the lane focused on the achiever lift.\\\\n2. The achiever equation holds at the SINGLE point z (per-point, matching BaseDivisor:143). Extending it across the whole piece D(h z) is brick 3 (RD-N read_sec_generates_stalk + h z \\\\u2208 ann(N z)), the SIBLING lane \\\\u2014 not this one.\\\\n3. The general-field keystone is A-parametric (any pole bound); the seed-prime one pins A := N \\\\u2212 d_p. Both consume Scheme.exists_achiever_of_span (BaseDivisorSpan) + divUniversalFibreKM_eq_span (Res:376) + divUniversalSeedFibreDivisor_spec (Fields:146). New import edge into Picard: RiemannRoch.BaseDivisorSpan.\\\\n\\\\nCommits: ab14a53d0 (core general-field lift), 4166521b9 (seed-prime d_p achiever). Both on refs/heads/main; touch only Picard/DivSchemeRedesignAchiever.lean + (ab14a53d0) the root import line.\\\",\\n      \\\"scope\\\": {\\n        \\\"projects\\\": [\\n          \\\"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild\\\"\\n        ]\\n      },\\n      \\\"audience\\\": \\\"horizon\\\",\\n      \\\"author\\\": \\\"human\\\",\\n      \\\"source_ref\\\": null,\\n      \\\"created_at\\\": \\\"2026-07-19T20:40:58.548388+00:00\\\",\\n      \\\"updated_at\\\": \\\"2026-07-19T20:40:58.548398+00:00\\\",\\n      \\\"comments\\\": [],\\n      \\\"metadata\\\": {\\n        \\\"history\\\": [\\n          {\\n            \\\"at\\\": \\\"2026-07-19T20:40:59.131070+00:00\\\",\\n            \\\"actor\\\": \\\"human\\\",\\n            \\\"field\\\": \\\"created\\\",\\n            \\\"from\\\": \\\"\\\",\\n            \\\"to\\\": \\\"open\\\",\\n            \\\"note\\\": \\\"opened\\\"\\n          }\\n        ]\\n      }\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"I-0290\\\",\\n      \\\"provider\\\": \\\"local\\\",\\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"info\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\",\\n      \\\"labels\\\": [\\n        \\\"agent-ready\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"body\\\": \\\"redesign brick 1 J-flat BUILD \\\\u2014 the (c4) reading-map cokernel R_Z-flatness exposed as a reusable keystone, reduced to the single carve input; genuine hspan_seedUniv (carve wiring at seedUniv) is the precisely-scoped residual (gated on redesigned seedUniv bricks 2-4 + the section->functionField germ bridge).\\\\n\\\\nNew file Picard/DivSchemeRedesignJFlat.lean (175 L). Single-module LEAN_NUM_THREADS=1 lake build GREEN under the mkdir lock (8672 jobs, 16s). All 3 keystones lean_verify axiom-clean [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]; zero sorries; zero new warnings (Pic.lean show-style + Challenge.lean sorries are pre-existing). Full-root stays green (leaf file). Root: HEAD-blob + own line only (sibling PicEtCrossBaseGraph line + Hinj-removal in working tree NOT swept; show --stat = my 2 paths, root +1).\\\\n\\\\n=== COMMIT (this lane) ===\\\\n- f033986c8  brick 1 J-flat: expose (c4) reading-map cokernel R_Z-flatness as a reusable keystone, reduced to the carve input\\\\n\\\\n=== KEYSTONES (VERBATIM; namespace AlgebraicGeometry.ThetaGeneratorSeed; section vars {k C R} {pi a} {K}, (D : ThetaGeneratorSeed C R pi a K); colength z := Gamma(relCurve C R, D.piece z) / Ideal.span {D.eqn z}; N z := D.sideColengthSubmodule z) ===\\\\n\\\\n(1) THE flat producer downstream RD-N (\\\\u00a71.3 input iii 'J z R_Z-flat') + certificate consume:\\\\n  forall_flat_colength_quotient_of_hsub (D) [Module.Finite R K]\\\\n    (hcolFin : forall z, Module.Finite R (colength z))\\\\n    (hcolFlat : forall z, Module.Flat R (colength z))\\\\n    (hsub : forall (z : relCurve C R) (p : PrimeSpectrum R),\\\\n      Function.Injective ((D.sideColengthSubmodule z).subtype.rTensor p.asIdeal.ResidueField))\\\\n    : forall z, Module.Flat R (colength z / D.sideColengthSubmodule z)\\\\n  \\\\u2014 hsub = the SINGLE genuine carve obligation: fibre non-collapse N z (x) kappa(p) into colength z (x) kappa(p) (rank-g pinning from divUniversal_carve_residueField). Composes landed hsub=>hinj (hinj_of_forall_sideColengthSubmodule_subtype_rTensor_injective, I-0286) + hinj=>hspan (hspan_of_forall_liftQ_rTensor_injective, I-0282) + c4.\\\\n\\\\n(2) forall_flat_colength_quotient_of_hspan (D) [Module.Finite R K] (hcolFin)(hcolFlat)\\\\n    (hspan : forall (z)(p : PrimeSpectrum R),\\\\n      LinearMap.ker (((D.kColengthMap z).comp K.subtype).rTensor p.asIdeal.ResidueField)\\\\n        <= LinearMap.range ((LinearMap.ker ((D.kColengthMap z).comp K.subtype)).subtype.rTensor p.asIdeal.ResidueField))\\\\n    : forall z, Module.Flat R (colength z / D.sideColengthSubmodule z)\\\\n  \\\\u2014 exact hflat argument of dvd_of_flat_quotient_of_field_vanishing (SeedDvd:128); hspan = the c4 (SlicingFlatKernel:296) hypothesis at L = ker f_z, hle = le_rfl.\\\\n\\\\n(3) flat_colength_quotient_of_hspan (D) (z) [Module.Finite R K] [Module.Finite R (colength z)] [Module.Flat R (colength z)] (hspan_z) : Module.Flat R (colength z / D.sideColengthSubmodule z)  \\\\u2014 single-point c4 wrapper.\\\\n\\\\n=== WHAT THIS IS ===\\\\ncolength z / N z ~= Gamma(D(h z)) / J.Gamma(D(h z)) (piecewise Gamma/J; eqn z = read(sec z) in J) \\\\u2014 the c4 conclusion of spec \\\\u00a71.4. From this the base ideal J itself is R_Z-flat as ker(Gamma -> Gamma/J) (Gamma flat, Gamma/J flat via SES) \\\\u2014 a cheap downstream step, NOT yet added here. Sound fibrewise-spanning route: NEVER the false FibreInjective (f_z (x) kappa always kills the seed section); the hspan/hsub route divides ker out first.\\\\n\\\\n=== RESIDUAL \\\\u2014 hsub_seedUniv (the genuine XL carve wall, UNCHANGED difficulty) ===\\\\nhsub at the concrete redesigned seedUniv: Function.Injective ((sideColengthSubmodule z).subtype.rTensor kappa(p)) via divUniversal_carve_residueField (FamilyUniv:135, carvePairArrow=0) transported by ker_baseChange_mkQ (DivCarveKit:91) + divUniversalFibreKM_eq_span (Res:376) + corank-g finrank_divUniversalFibreKM_add (AssembleKappa:207). BLOCKER = the still-UNBUILT section->functionField germ bridge (relThetaResSide on D(h') <-> thetaFieldRead) identifying the piece colength fibre with the fibre-window reading (I-0286), which depends on the redesigned (sec z, h z) of bricks 2-4. This file takes hsub/hspan as HYPOTHESES so the flat conclusion is non-circular and stable under that redesign; the carve wiring instantiates them downstream. No FibreInjective (dead). No sorries; full-root green.\\\",\\n      \\\"scope\\\": {\\n        \\\"projects\\\": [\\n          \\\"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild\\\"\\n        ]\\n      },\\n      \\\"audience\\\": \\\"horizon\\\",\\n      \\\"author\\\": \\\"horizon\\\",\\n      \\\"source_ref\\\": null,\\n      \\\"created_at\\\": \\\"2026-07-19T20:15:19.970298+00:00\\\",\\n      \\\"updated_at\\\": \\\"2026-07-19T20:15:19.970308+00:00\\\",\\n      \\\"comments\\\": [],\\n      \\\"metadata\\\": {\\n        \\\"agent\\\": \\\"dd4-redesign-brick1-jflat-lane\\\",\\n        \\\"history\\\": [\\n          {\\n            \\\"at\\\": \\\"2026-07-19T20:15:20.550533+00:00\\\",\\n            \\\"actor\\\": \\\"horizon\\\",\\n            \\\"field\\\": \\\"created\\\",\\n            \\\"from\\\": \\\"\\\",\\n            \\\"to\\\": \\\"open\\\",\\n            \\\"note\\\": \\\"opened\\\"\\n          }\\n        ]\\n      }\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"I-0289\\\",\\n      \\\"provider\\\": \\\"local\\\",\\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"info\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\",\\n      \\\"labels\\\": [\\n        \\\"agent-ready\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"body\\\": \\\"DD-4 redesign feasibility: HARD-BUT-BUILDABLE (sound, unblockable, ~2 XL + 3 L + 2 M bricks, multi-week; NO impossibility). Worksheet informal/spec-dd4-redesign.md, commit 6e35e7ea3d48d9361353d0ed6fcbaf15e0cb236d.\\\\n\\\\n=== THE DECISIVE ANSWER (task Q1b: does a carve-direct NON-seed relDivisor dissolve the achiever-lift?) ===\\\\nThe achiever-lift (I-0258) dissolves EITHER WAY, so skipping the seed buys nothing and costs more. KEEP THE SEED; redesign (sec z, h z). A fully carve-direct non-seed CertifiedDivisorFamily (build base ideal J as a Module.Invertible line bundle over Gamma(relCurve), read off LocalEquations.eqn) IS possible but strictly HARDER: it needs THREE bridges ABSENT in mathlib+in-tree \\\\u2014 (i) R-flat + fibrewise-invertible => invertible, (ii) rank-1 projective => Module.Invertible (mathlib has NO converse), (iii) invertible ideal => single local generator J.Gamma_f = span{eqn}. All three are Gamma-LOCAL (curve-local), whereas every landed engine (SlicingFlatKernel, SupportTubeFinite, the carve) is R_Z-FIBREWISE. The seed route reaches the SAME local generator via R_Z-fibrewise flatness + a one-point stalk Nakayama, reusing maximal landed surface.\\\\n\\\\n=== WHY THE ACHIEVER-LIFT IS NOT ACTUALLY A WALL (dissolves I-0258/I-0288 (A)) ===\\\\nsec z = a relative achiever AT z, built by lifting a kappa(p)-fibre achiever THROUGH the SURJECTION read (x) kappa(p) : K_univ (x) kappa(p) ->> H0(N - d_p) (divUniversalFibreKM_eq_span, DivSchemeSeedUnivRes:376) + exists_coeffAt_eq_baseDivisorAt (BaseDivisor:143). I-0258 is TRUE (a single window vector need not reduce to a CHOSEN f_p) but IRRELEVANT: we need SOME achiever, and the surjection hits every element of the window. A clean lift, not the non-liftable step the history feared.\\\\n\\\\n=== THE FIBRE-CUTTER (dissolves I-0288 (B)) ===\\\\nh z is NOT algebraMap f (base-only; makes D(h) the WHOLE fibre chart, exactly why I-0288 hle failed). Instead h z in ann(N z), N z := J/(read sec z) finite over R_Z (SupportTubeFinite, I-0244), at z not in supp(N z). ann(N z) elements are GENUINE fibre-cutters. NOTE: probe found NO fibre-cutter over general R exists in-tree \\\\u2014 only PointDivisor over a FIELD base (PointDivisor:190/278); ann(N z) is the in-tree route to a relative cutter.\\\\n\\\\n=== THE ONE GENUINE WALL + SIZES ===\\\\nRD-N (relative-local-BPF stalk Nakayama, size L): read(sec z) generates J at stalk O_z from fibre generation + J R_Z-FLAT. Flatness load-bearing (J cap pGamma = pJ, no Tor_1) \\\\u2014 WITHOUT it the k[eps] trap (I-0231) fires. Then hdvd on D(h z) is DIRECT (feed simpler isGenerator_of_fibre_ne_zero, DivSchemeSeed:188, NOT the fibrewise-ker-span capstone). Prerequisite (size XL, largest lane): J R_Z-flat via SlicingFlatKernel c4 (:296) on the reading map read, fed by divUniversal_carve_residueField (FamilyUniv:135) \\\\u2014 I-0284 hspan content, cleaner (no chosen eqn z). Then no-leak from proper support (I-0285 reduction), certificate non-circular (dvd holds), divUniversalFamily := divFamEps_certifiedFamily (DivSchemeEps:312) = DDR9-U U1.\\\\n\\\\nFile plan (anti-circular, dvd BEFORE certificate): (1) J-flat XL -> (2) achiever M -> (3) RD-N/hdvd L -> (4) seed/isGenerator M -> (5) no-leak L -> (6) certificate L -> (7) U1 L.\\\\n\\\\nFallback if (1)/(3) wall: the fully carve-direct non-seed family (needs the 3 absent Gamma-local bridges) or Sym^g/Hilbert plan-B. Supersedes I-0268 spec-dd4-seam.md whose relDivisor routed through seedUniv.localEquations (I-0272).\\\",\\n      \\\"scope\\\": {\\n        \\\"projects\\\": [\\n          \\\"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild\\\"\\n        ]\\n      },\\n      \\\"audience\\\": \\\"horizon\\\",\\n      \\\"author\\\": \\\"agent\\\",\\n      \\\"source_ref\\\": null,\\n      \\\"created_at\\\": \\\"2026-07-19T19:58:11.251458+00:00\\\",\\n      \\\"updated_at\\\": \\\"2026-07-19T19:58:11.251468+00:00\\\",\\n      \\\"comments\\\": [],\\n      \\\"metadata\\\": {\\n        \\\"agent\\\": \\\"dd4-redesign-feasibility-lane\\\",\\n        \\\"history\\\": [\\n          {\\n            \\\"at\\\": \\\"2026-07-19T19:58:11.829922+00:00\\\",\\n            \\\"actor\\\": \\\"agent\\\",\\n            \\\"field\\\": \\\"created\\\",\\n            \\\"from\\\": \\\"\\\",\\n            \\\"to\\\": \\\"open\\\",\\n            \\\"note\\\": \\\"opened\\\"\\n          }\\n        ]\\n      }\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"I-0288\\\",\\n      \\\"provider\\\": \\\"local\\\",\\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"info\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\",\\n      \\\"labels\\\": [\\n        \\\"agent-ready\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"body\\\": \\\"BPF/no-leak crux (G-4 seed / DD-4 seam): NO-REDESIGN. The current seedUniv section/piece choice CANNOT support the hfield lower bound (hle) or the hcolFin no-leak. DESIGN ESCALATION (seedUniv.sec + seedUniv.h in DivSchemeSeedUnivGen.lean need revision). No Lean written, no sorries, nothing committed \\\\u2014 verdict is analytic, grounded entirely in LANDED lemmas (same discipline as I-0260). The germ bridge (I-0287) did NOT dissolve the wall; it sharpened/moved it but it persists, rooted in the same sec defect as I-0258/I-0260.\\\\n\\\\n=== THE DECISIVE OBSTRUCTION (3 verified facts force NO) ===\\\\n\\\\n(1) The fibre window is HIGH-DIMENSIONAL, never 1-dim. dim_kappa(p) divUniversalFibreKM = h0(O(N)) - g = deg N + 1 - 2g (finrank_divUniversalFibreKM_add, AssembleKappa:207, + h0=degN+1-g via subsingleton_h1_windowN). deg N = M*delta with M*delta >= b + 2g + (g+2)(s+1)delta (windowM_spec WindowLedger:189 + deg_windowN WindowFieldTransport:319). Since delta>=1 and (g+2)(s+1)delta>=2, dim >= 2 robustly (typically much more). So the \\\\\\\"1-dim => trivial span\\\\\\\" YES-escape is CLOSED: readings of K_univ span the whole >=2-dim window (divUniversalFibreKM_eq_span, Res:376), so read(sec) (one element) must DIVIDE a >=2-dim family of readings on D(h').\\\\n\\\\n(2) seedUniv.h z = algebraMap f is a BASE-RING pullback (Gen:289, f in R_Z from exists_forall_windowCompare_ne_zero). By relPinnedSectionsMap_algebraMap_eq (Facts:212), base-change to kappa(p) gives algebraMap(f mod p); for f not-in p (i.e. p in D(f), incl. basePrime(germ_z) and its whole D(f)-nbhd) f mod p != 0 is a UNIT in the field kappa(p), so its basicOpen is top. Hence D(h') = the ENTIRE pinned fibre chart over kappa(p). ZERO FIBREWISE SHRINK ROOM \\\\u2014 the YES-branch escape (\\\\\\\"extra vanishing avoidable by shrinking h z\\\\\\\") is STRUCTURALLY IMPOSSIBLE for h z = algebraMap f: it shrinks the base only, never the fibre.\\\\n\\\\n(3) The germ-bridge residual hle (relThetaResSide_mem_span_of_forall_ord_le, DivSchemeUnivFibreHdiv.lean:203-211) needs, with s:=Theta(windowCompare x_psi), t:=Theta(windowCompare x_sec):  for every closed w in D(h'), ord(read psi)_w <= ord(read sec)_w. Upper bound available: ord(read psi)_w <= B_w := divisorBound(windowN - d_p)_w for ALL w (divFamPhi_windowCompare_mem, Res:423 + divUniversalSeedFibreDivisor_spec, Fields:146). So hle <=> read(sec) ACHIEVES the ceiling ord(read sec)_w = B_w at EVERY w of D(h') = the whole chart. But seedUniv.sec z = relThetaWindowEquiv x carries ONLY windowCompare(kappa(p),x) != 0 (Gen:300, exists_sec_windowCompare_ne_zero_seedPrime) = \\\\\\\"read(sec) != 0 as a fibre section\\\\\\\", NO minimal-vanishing/achiever data. A generic nonzero element of H0(windowN - d_p) has deg(windowN - d_p) = deg N - g > 0 EXTRA zeros (moving part) landing generically INSIDE the chart. At any extra-zero w0, ord(read sec)_{w0} < B_{w0} while some psi (readings span the window) hits B_{w0} => hle FAILS. windowCompare!=0 does not even prevent an extra zero AT z itself.\\\\n\\\\n=== SAME defect kills hcolFin (no-leak) ===\\\\npiece z = D(h z), eqn z = read(sec) (Family:93,113). no-leak = closure(piece cap V(read sec)) subset piece. With h = base pullback, piece = chart cap phi^-1(D(f)) (whole fibre over D(f)); read(sec)'s relative zero locus leaks to special fibres over boundary of D(f) \\\\u2014 EXACTLY I-0285's toy counterexample (P1/k[t], {x=t}, piece D(t): trace leaks to (0,0) not in piece, colength k[t,1/t] not R-finite). windowCompare!=0 (fibrewise nonvanishing) is insufficient, as I-0285 already found. hfield and hcolFin share the root cause.\\\\n\\\\n=== WHY the germ bridge (I-0287) did NOT save it ===\\\\nIt reduced the RELATIVE hfield to a FIBREWISE ord inequality \\\\u2014 genuine progress that sidesteps I-0260's \\\\\\\"fibrewise-does-not-lift-to-relative\\\\\\\" objection (that content now lives in the flatness/carve clauses hcolFlat/hspan). But the fibrewise inequality STILL demands read(sec) be a fibre BPF-achiever, and because D(h')=whole chart it means achievement on the ENTIRE chart. The wall moved (relative-generation -> fibrewise-achievement-on-the-whole-chart) but persists.\\\\n\\\\n=== WHAT seedUniv MUST BECOME (the redesign, orchestrator matter) ===\\\\nBOTH pointwise fields need revision (currently sec=windowCompare!=0 lift, h=algebraMap base-pullback):\\\\n (A) sec z := a RELATIVE ACHIEVER in K_univ=divUniversalSeedK whose kappa(p)-fibre reading achieves the base divisor bd=d_p at z (field-level per-point achiever exists_coeffAt_eq_baseDivisorAt, BaseDivisor:143, LIFTED to a relative R_Z-section inside K_univ) \\\\u2014 so z is NOT an extra zero. This achiever-lift is I-0258's flagged generally-NON-liftable step (a single R_Z window vector need not reduce to a chosen kappa(p)-combination f; windowCompare(W) is only an R_Z/p-semilinear image whose kappa(p)-span, not itself, is the window). It is the DD-4 base-field-transport / relative-BPF seam I-0260 recommended (DivSchemeFamily:44); FIELD-level BPF infra (BpfSpan, BaseDivisorSpan) has NO relative/R_Z version.\\\\n (B) h z := a genuine CURVE section cutting a fibre-neighbourhood of z (NOT algebraMap of a base element), so D(h') shrinks in the fibre to a punctured nbhd of z that excludes read(sec)'s OTHER extra zeros. Only then does read(sec) meet B_w on all of D(h'), giving hle; and V(eqn z)=d_p's branch through z becomes proper/contained, giving hcolFin.\\\\n\\\\n=== STATUS ===\\\\nhdiv_seedUniv / seedUniv_hfield / hnoleak_seedUniv: NONE present (grep-confirmed absent), NONE landed \\\\u2014 correctly so; a bridge-sec seed would BAKE IN a sec for which hle/hcolFin are unprovable. Germ bridge (15d9eb465) + shared brick (2b6b00cf5) + hcolFin reduction (4ec2a0d60/819f9dbc2) remain valid and forward-compatible \\\\u2014 they consume WHATEVER sec the redesign produces. The ONE pointwise residual (hle at every closed w of D(h')) is now razor-isolated; discharged the instant seedUniv.sec becomes a relative achiever and seedUniv.h a fibre-cutter. Verdict