ngs in my file.\\\\n\\\\nSHARED PLUS-CLASS COLLAPSE LEMMA (the name B-4 consumes) \\\\u2014 KEYSTONE 1 (verbatim):\\\\ntheorem PicEtAff.map_mk_eq_unit_of_algHom {K L : Type u} [Field K] [Algebra k K] [Field L] [Algebra k L] [Algebra K L] [IsScalarTower k K L] {E : Algebra.EtaleCover K} (x : descentClasses C E) (l : E.Carrier -a[K] L) : PicEtAff.map C L (PicEtAff.mk C E x) = PicEtAff.unit C L (relPicAlgMap C (l.restrictScalars k) (x : relPic C (overSpec k E.Carrier)))\\\\nContext: {k}[Field k](C : Over (Spec (.of k))) ONLY \\\\u2014 NO hypotheses on C.hom (pure plus construction). Proof: map_mk reads the L-restriction as mk(E.baseChange L)(descentBaseChange x); unit_eq_mk reads the target unit on the same cover; the descent/cocycle condition relPicAlgMap_congr (baseChangeInclude vs ofId comp l, through descentBaseChange_coe) identifies the two descent classes. The honest class is relPicAlgMap l x, EXACTLY the degAff_mk honest class (DegreeZero.lean:273).\\\\n\\\\nKEYSTONE 2 (verbatim, Cech form the degree seam + exists_cechPicClass_eq consume):\\\\ntheorem PicEtAff.map_mk_eq_unit_relPicMk_of_algHom {K L : Type u} [Field K] [Algebra k K] [Field L] [Algebra k L] [Algebra K L] [IsScalarTower k K L] {E : Algebra.EtaleCover K} (x : descentClasses C E) (l : E.Carrier -a[K] L) : exists M : (C (X) overSpec k L).left.CechPic, PicEtAff.map C L (PicEtAff.mk C E x) = PicEtAff.unit C L (relPicMk C (overSpec k L) M)\\\\nProof: relPicMk_surjective on the honest class + keystone 1.\\\\n\\\\nHOW B-4 / B-5 CONSUME IT: write the fibre plus class as mk E x (PicEtAff.ind / picEtAffineEquiv); field cofinality Algebra.EtaleCover.exists_finiteSeparableField_algHom (EtaleCover.lean:287) gives L finite separable + l : E.Carrier -a[K] L; apply keystone 1/2. The L/K/k tower is a CLEAN instance hypothesis (campaign-idiomatic, cf DivSchemeSeed.lean:73). Well-definedness across splittings = E-iv-alg + ClassCohomology:111 (not re-derived here).\\\\n\\\\nNEW WALL / GOTCHA (verified this pass, MEMORY-WORTHY for B-4/B-5/B-6): the I-0236 two-level-tower diamond is a GENUINE whnf NON-TERMINATION (not merely slow \\\\u2014 still times out at 1,000,000 heartbeats). Instantiating L with a RingHom.toAlgebra composite letI (letI : Algebra k L := ((algebraMap K L).comp (algebraMap k K)).toAlgebra, the DegreeZero.lean:339 pattern) EXPLODES the moment PicEtAff.map C L unfolds the base-changed etale carrier (a MvPolynomial-quotient). This is why the collapse is stated with the tower as CLEAN hypotheses and NOT bundled as an existential over-instances of a cofinality-produced L. degAff_mul survives the same composite letI only because degAff never forms map/baseChange. CONSEQUENCE: B-5 coverage step 1 and B-4 link-2 (etale-carrier image transport) MUST supply the fibre extension L via a NATIVE k-algebra tower (residue-field-based instances), never a composite letI, or they hit this wall. respectTransparency false + maxSynthPendingDepth 3 do NOT fix it.\\\\n\\\\nC9 / divRep BOUNDARY (where B-5 stops, per worksheet): chartLocus is still UNDEFINED (DAT-C C9 unshipped, confirmed I-0252). Therefore COV-1 pic0_chartLocus_cover CANNOT YET BE STATED. Its target predicate is the witness/h1=0 form of Pic0ChartLocusOpen keystone isOpen_setOf_exists_witness_h1_vanishing (9469ecd63). Restated pointwise it still needs: (a) chartLocus (C9); (b) the fibre-restriction of the pic0 class to kappa(t) then to the separable L (my collapse keystones \\\\u2014 but see the diamond wall: the restriction forces a fibre-field k-tower that must be native); (c) the degree/choose-m/kill-h1/greedy-drop(B-1)/density(B-2)/package chain. Pins for the coverage core: degAt_pic0_mul_pow (DegreeSeam:145), degAt_chartValue (C5), exists_bound_subsingleton_hModule_one_of_isFinite_toP1 at L (UniformVanishing:71), exists_effective_sub_h0_eq_one (B-1, CoverageDrop), Over.dense_baseChange_rationalPoints (B-2). B-6 (IsLocallySurjective instance) unchanged \\\\u2014 still divRep-gated.\\\\n\\\\nDEVIATIONS vs worksheet s1.2 step 1: (1) the collapse is stated as map_mk_eq_unit_of_algHom (explicit l + clean tower) rather than an existential-bundled restriction \\\\u2014 forced by the diamond wall; the exists-over-instances form is mathematically fine but un-elaborable with a composite letI. (2) The picEtAffineEquiv/PicEtAff.mk read (worksheet step-1 preamble) is left to the consumer; the collapse operates on a PicEtAff C K element directly.\\\",\\n      \\\"scope\\\": {\\n        \\\"projects\\\": [\\n          \\\"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild\\\"\\n        ]\\n      },\\n      \\\"audience\\\": \\\"horizon\\\",\\n      \\\"author\\\": \\\"human\\\",\\n      \\\"source_ref\\\": null,\\n      \\\"created_at\\\": \\\"2026-07-19T11:52:39.030589+00:00\\\",\\n      \\\"updated_at\\\": \\\"2026-07-19T11:52:39.030600+00:00\\\",\\n      \\\"comments\\\": [],\\n      \\\"metadata\\\": {\\n        \\\"history\\\": [\\n          {\\n            \\\"at\\\": \\\"2026-07-19T11:52:39.509320+00:00\\\",\\n            \\\"actor\\\": \\\"human\\\",\\n            \\\"field\\\": \\\"created\\\",\\n            \\\"from\\\": \\\"\\\",\\n            \\\"to\\\": \\\"open\\\",\\n            \\\"note\\\": \\\"opened\\\"\\n          }\\n        ]\\n      }\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"I-0252\\\",\\n      \\\"provider\\\": \\\"local\\\",\\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"info\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\",\\n      \\\"labels\\\": [\\n        \\\"agent-ready\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"body\\\": \\\"CHART-U(b) partial \\\\u2014 datum-level witness-locus openness + transport(ii) topological half LANDED (fresh start, predecessor died in survey)\\\\n\\\\nFILE: MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild/AlgebraicJacobian/Picard/Pic0ChartLocusOpen.lean (137 L). Commits: 9469ecd63 (core), 461da4972 (transport). Root-wired (HEAD-blob + only my line, protocol s4). Zero sorries; every keystone axiom-clean [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]; single-module LEAN_NUM_THREADS=1 lake green under mkdir lock (8864 jobs); zero warnings in my file.\\\\n\\\\nKEYSTONE 1 (verbatim) \\\\u2014 the datum-level heart of CHART-U(b), engine-open in the chartLocus witness form:\\\\ntheorem BasicOpenCocycleDatum.isOpen_setOf_exists_witness_h1_vanishing (D : BasicOpenCocycleDatum C B \\\\u03c0) (h\\\\u03c0 : \\\\u03c0 \\\\u226b P1.structureMap k = C.hom) : IsOpen {q : PrimeSpectrum B | \\\\u2203 W : ((C \\\\u2297 overSpec k q.asIdeal.ResidueField).left).CurveDivisor, Scheme.CurveDivisor.picClass q.asIdeal.ResidueField W = Scheme.CechPic.map (relCurveMap C B q.asIdeal.ResidueField) D.cechPicClass \\\\u2227 Subsingleton (Sheaf.HModule ((C \\\\u2297 overSpec k q.asIdeal.ResidueField).left.divisorSheaf q.asIdeal.ResidueField W) 1)}\\\\nProof = datumRigidEngine_isOpen_vanishing (Noetherian-free engine, dat-d s3.5) read through C1's two-way dictionary BasicOpenCocycleDatum.subsingleton_h1_tensor_iff_exists_witness (GAP-6): the engine complex-form fibre cond Subsingleton(H1(pair D) \\\\u2297[B] \\\\u03ba(q)) is pointwise the effective-witness/h1=0 cond. Class-intrinsic. Context: [IsFinite \\\\u03c0][SmoothOfRelativeDimension 1 C.hom][IsProper C.hom][GeometricallyIrreducible C.hom].\\\\n\\\\nKEYSTONE 2/3 (verbatim) \\\\u2014 CHART-U(b) transport (ii) topological half, the 'one IsOpenMap application' of w4-datb s1.6:\\\\ntheorem isOpen_of_isOpen_preimage_of_isOpenMap_surjective {X Y : Type*} [TopologicalSpace X] [TopologicalSpace Y] {f : X \\\\u2192 Y} (hcont : Continuous f) (hopen : IsOpenMap f) (hsurj : Function.Surjective f) {V : Set Y} (hV : IsOpen (f \\\\u207b\\\\u00b9' V)) : IsOpen V\\\\ntheorem isOpen_of_isOpen_comap_preimage {R S : Type u} [CommRing R] [CommRing S] (f : R \\\\u2192+* S) (hopen : IsOpenMap (PrimeSpectrum.comap f)) (hsurj : Function.Surjective (PrimeSpectrum.comap f)) {V : Set (PrimeSpectrum R)} (hV : IsOpen (PrimeSpectrum.comap f \\\\u207b\\\\u00b9' V)) : IsOpen V\\\\nProof = mathlib IsOpenMap.isQuotientMap + IsQuotientMap.isOpen_preimage (+ PrimeSpectrum.continuous_comap).\\\\n\\\\nAMENDMENT COMPLIANCE (I-0248 / I-0251): built against the DAT-C frozen interface AS AMENDED. (a-amendment, split predicate for arbitrary plus classes): honored \\\\u2014 the witness locus is stated in the effective-witness/h1=0 (dimension/witness) form; no reliance on chartValue-collapse, so it covers arbitrary plus classes. (b-amendment, pinned openness chain): the chain is realized as pinned \\\\u2014 extraction\\\\u2192(shifted datum)\\\\u2192RE-5-free engine (C1 made the engine Noetherian-free, so the RE-5/transport-(i) descent is OBVIATED for openness; recorded) \\\\u2192 witness-form openness (keystone 1) \\\\u2192 transport (ii) topological (keystones 2/3). NOTE for orchestrator: the C1 landing made datumRigidEngine_isOpen_vanishing Noetherian-free, so transport (i) (Spec B\\\\u2192Spec B0 RE-5 preimage) is NOT needed on the openness path \\\\u2014 one fewer unlanded link than the worksheet chain lists.\\\\n\\\\nREMAINING GAPS (the wall \\\\u2014 two links, honest): (1) the shifted-datum CONSTRUCTOR's class arithmetic: form the honest carrier class c=\\\\u03bb|_B collapse (picEtAffineEquiv\\\\u2192PicEtAff.mk E x\\\\u2192\\\\u00e9tale field-cofinality), then the shifted CechPic c\\\\u00b7\\\\u03b8^m\\\\u00b7[\\\\u03a3]\\\\u207b\\\\u00b9 (theta layer cechPicClass_thetaChartDatum + C0 GAP-1 inverse datum DivisorAdaptation.divisorDatum/.inv), then extract via exists_cechPicClass_eq to instantiate keystone 1's D. The class-multiply-and-extract shell is a thin wrapper over exists_cechPicClass_eq; the genuine content is the \\\\u03a3/\\\\u03b8 naturality proving the datum's fibre class at \\\\u03ba(t) equals \\\\u03bb_t\\\\u00b7\\\\u03b8^m\\\\u00b7(\\\\u2212\\\\u03a3) \\\\u2014 DAT-C-owned vocab (chartValue, ThetaShift), risk of getting the shift wrong is why it is left as a pinned wall not a guess. (2) transport (ii) HARD half \\\\u2014 the fibre-field invariance identifying (PrimeSpectrum.comap f)\\\\u207b\\\\u00b9(chartLocus over A) =