\\n      \\\"comments\\\": [],\\n      \\\"metadata\\\": {\\n        \\\"history\\\": [\\n          {\\n            \\\"at\\\": \\\"2026-07-19T11:14:44.281255+00:00\\\",\\n            \\\"actor\\\": \\\"human\\\",\\n            \\\"field\\\": \\\"created\\\",\\n            \\\"from\\\": \\\"\\\",\\n            \\\"to\\\": \\\"open\\\",\\n            \\\"note\\\": \\\"opened\\\"\\n          }\\n        ]\\n      }\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"I-0226\\\",\\n      \\\"provider\\\": \\\"local\\\",\\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"info\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\",\\n      \\\"labels\\\": [\\n        \\\"agent-ready\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"body\\\": \\\"W7-A1 PARTIAL (lane w7-a1, Opus 4.8, commit ea4ed5c97): datum-level baseChange_ofCurve REDUCED to a single Leg-4 core, not yet fully landed. New Picard/JacobianDataBaseChangeAbel.lean (166L, axiom-clean [propext,Classical.choice,Quot.sound], root-wired).\\\\n\\\\nR-K1-3 ACCESSOR RE-PIN (verified vs B-6b committed sig e30e066a1): the worksheet's .hom.hom.hom is CORRECT. baseChangeIsoOfData d dL : (baseChange k L).mapGrp.obj (.mk d.J) \\\\u2245 .mk dL.J in Grp(Over(Spec L)); underlying scheme morphism (baseChange k L).obj d.J \\\\u27f6 dL.J is .hom.hom.hom (iso .hom -> Grp-mor, Mon-mor .hom, underlying .hom). L is IMPLICIT (from dL). Bridge lemma landed:\\\\n  baseChangeIsoOfData_hom_hom_hom : (baseChangeIsoOfData d dL).hom.hom.hom = ((d.baseChange L).uniqueUpToIso dL).hom\\\\nREUSABLE by DAT-J: the equation reducing the frozen baseChangeIso to uniqueUpToIso.\\\\n\\\\nFULL REDUCTION LANDED (baseChange_ofCurve_data_of_core, axiom-clean, modulo hCore): dL.homEquiv injectivity -> accessor bridge -> homEquiv_uniqueUpToIso_hom -> (d.baseChange L).homEquiv unfolds DEFEQ (rfl) to (pic0CrossBaseEquiv...).symm \\\\u2218 d.homEquiv \\\\u2218 (mapPullbackAdj \\\\u03c3 transpose); transpose of (baseChange k L).map aj = (counit.app C) \\\\u226b aj by counit_naturality; homEquiv_comp -> pic0Map C \\\\u03b5C (abelElement C P). Seam crossings term-mode only.\\\\n\\\\nREMAINING = hCore (ONLY gap), Leg-4 '\\\\u03b8 carries the Abel class across the base-field shuffle':\\\\n  (pic0CrossBaseEquiv k L C C_L).symm (pic0Map C ((Over.mapPullbackAdj (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap k L)))).counit.app C) (abelElement C P)) = abelElement C_L (Functor.LaxMonoidal.\\\\u03b5 (baseChange k L) \\\\u226b (baseChange k L).map P)\\\\nUnderlying picEt (Subtype.ext + pic0CrossBaseEquiv_symm_apply_coe + pic0Map_coe + abelElement_coe + abelPicEt_map):\\\\n  picEtCrossBase k L C C_L (picEtMap C \\\\u03b5C (abelPicEt C P)) = abelPicEt C_L Q,  Q = \\\\u03b5 \\\\u226b (baseChange k L).map P.\\\\nCONFIRMED no existing picEtCrossBase\\\\u2194relPicToPicEt/relPicMk bridge at general (non-affine) tests (relPicCrossBase is affine-only). Needs new infra: (A) picEtCrossBase commutes with the \\\\u00e9tale unit relPicToPicEt\\\\u2218relPicMk at a general test (componentwise sectionShuffle vs relPic gluing), then (B) base-field-change of the graph class via abelPicEt_map + graphLocalEquations_base_change (recon \\\\u00a73.4).\\\\n\\\\nFINISH: prove hCore, then baseChange_ofCurve_data := baseChange_ofCurve_data_of_core hCore (frozen worksheet-\\\\u00a73 shape); add \\\\\\\\leanok blueprint node in Jacobian.tex after def:baseChangeIsoOfData; set AJCR.w7-functor.a1 done. Blueprint node DEFERRED this session (dishonest \\\\\\\\leanok while conditional). DAT-J closures baseChangeIso_id/_comp + frozen baseChange_ofCurve remain Fleet A.\\\",\\n      \\\"scope\\\": {\\n        \\\"projects\\\": [\\n          \\\"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild\\\"\\n        ]\\n      },\\n      \\\"audience\\\": \\\"horizon\\\",\\n      \\\"author\\\": \\\"human\\\",\\n      \\\"source_ref\\\": null,\\n      \\\"created_at\\\": \\\"2026-07-17T17:25:05.037586+00:00\\\",\\n      \\\"updated_at\\\": \\\"2026-07-17T17:25:05.037599+00:00\\\",\\n      \\\"comments\\\": [],\\n      \\\"metadata\\\": {\\n        \\\"history\\\": [\\n          {\\n            \\\"at\\\": \\\"2026-07-17T17:25:05.455349+00:00\\\",\\n            \\\"actor\\\": \\\"human\\\",\\n            \\\"field\\\": \\\"created\\\",\\n            \\\"from\\\": \\\"\\\",\\n            \\\"to\\\": \\\"open\\\",\\n            \\\"note\\\": \\\"opened\\\"\\n          }\\n        ]\\n      }\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"I-0218\\\",\\n      \\\"provider\\\": \\\"local\\\",\\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"memory\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\",\\n      \\\"labels\\\": [\\n        \\\"agent-ready\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"body\\\": \\\"Model switch mid-run 2026-07-17 ~22:20: Fable 5 usage exhausted, fleet moved to Opus 4.8\\\\n\\\\nThe horizon-fable5 harness's Fable-5 budget was exhausted around 22:15 (three lanes \\\\u2014 B-56, K-1 worksheet, m33-blueprint \\\\u2014 died simultaneously during orientation on 'You've reached your Fable 5 limit'). The interactive orchestrator switched to Opus 4.8 (1M context) and relaunched all three. CONVENTION CHANGE for Opus-authored commits: the private-index+CAS commit trailer is now 'Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>' instead of the protocol doc's literal 'Claude Fable 5' \\\\u2014 this is a deliberate honesty fix, the 'Archon-Commit: agent' provenance trailer and everything else in protocol-concurrent-lanes.md \\\\u00a71 is unchanged. The ledger therefore has a Fable-5\\\\u2192Opus trailer boundary around commit 6f279d7ca (last Fable-authored) / the 22:20 relaunch. Do not 'correct' older Fable-5 trailers.\\\",\\n      \\\"scope\\\": {\\n        \\\"projects\\\": [\\n          \\\"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild\\\"\\n        ]\\n      },\\n      \\\"audience\\\": \\\"horizon\\\",\\n      \\\"author\\\": \\\"human\\\",\\n      \\\"source_ref\\\": null,\\n      \\\"created_at\\\": \\\"2026-07-17T14:21:56.144332+00:00\\\",\\n      \\\"updated_at\\\": \\\"2026-07-17T14:21:56.144342+00:00\\\",\\n      \\\"comments\\\": [],\\n      \\\"metadata\\\": {\\n        \\\"history\\\": [\\n          {\\n            \\\"at\\\": \\\"2026-07-17T14:21:56.547206+00:00\\\",\\n            \\\"actor\\\": \\\"human\\\",\\n            \\\"field\\\": \\\"created\\\",\\n            \\\"from\\\": \\\"\\\",\\n            \\\"to\\\": \\\"open\\\",\\n            \\\"note\\\": \\\"opened\\\"\\n          }\\n        ]\\n      }\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"I-0209\\\",\\n      \\\"provider\\\": \\\"local\\\",\\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"memory\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\",\\n      \\\"labels\\\": [\\n        \\\"agent-ready\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"body\\\": \\\"THE Z-CLOPEN CERTIFICATE PRINCIPLE (DD-1/DD-2 lanes, 2026-07-17 \\\\u2014 three independent sightings in one day; treat as a standing design constraint for every DAT-D brick).\\\\n\\\\nA DivisorAdaptation piece carries an R-finite-projective colength \\\\u2014 clause (c1) of IsCertified \\\\u2014 IFF the piece's trace on the divisor scheme Z = V(D) (finite flat over Spec R) is CLOPEN in Z. Any construction that slices Z along the base (basic-open refinement of pieces, denominator-cleared pieces from a localization cover, Z-blind extraction) produces section rings like R_u that are NOT finite over R, and the certificate is unrecoverable \\\\u2014 the localization-span descent lemmas' hypotheses are FALSE, not merely hard. Canonical counterexample: R = k[u], zero-section divisor, cleared piece D(u-tilde): colength = R_u.\\\\n\\\\nConsequences adjudicated today: (1) the DD-1 pt-transport seam could NOT be fixed by extraction + certificate transport (certificates are not refinement-stable) \\\\u2014 fixed instead by the S1 carrier surgery (point-free eqn_rel, total mapAlg, commit 19c79359); (2) DD-2 S5's glued adaptation could NOT take its certificate from denominator-cleared pieces (spec-dd-2 section-5 route corrected in the addendum) \\\\u2014 the gluing keystone landed CONDITIONAL on hcert (exists_glue_of_away_compat_of_certifiedRep, commit 1758fad90).\\\\n\\\\nTHE MISSING BRICK (next in the DD-2 lane; coordinate with DD-R before speccing \\\\u2014 same substrate as DDR-4's engine bridge, spec-dd-r section-7 risk 1): W-as-algebra extraction \\\\u2014 the glued colength W(d) of a certified family is a finite projective R-ALGEBRA (= Gamma(Z)); its canonical idempotents (glued via the module-localization sheaf sequence over the away cover) split Z into packets; CRT-separated chart generators give packet-swallowing basic-open pieces whose traces are clopen; that adaptation carries the certificate and discharges hcert, upgrading the conditional keystone to the pinned DivFam.exists_glue_of_away_compat. Only then can S6 deliver divFunctor at full strength for DDR-9.\\\",\\n      \\\"scope\\\": {\\n        \\\"projects\\\": [\\n          \\\"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild\\\"\\n        ]\\n      },\\n      \\\"audience\\\": \\\"horizon\\\",\\n      \\\"author\\\": \\\"horizon\\\",\\n      \\\"source_ref\\\": null,\\n      \\\"created_at\\\": \\\"2026-07-17T09:48:15.292906+00:00\\\",\\n      \\\"updated_at\\\": \\\"2026-07-17T09:48:15.292916+00:00\\\",\\n      \\\"comments\\\": [],\\n      \\\"metadata\\\": {\\n        \\\"history\\\": [\\n          {\\n            \\\"at\\\": \\\"2026-07-17T09:48:15.695858+00:00\\\",\\n            \\\"actor\\\": \\\"horizon\\\",\\n            \\\"field\\\": \\\"created\\\",\\n            \\\"from\\\": \\\"\\\",\\n            \\\"to\\\": \\\"open\\\",\\n            \\\"note\\\": \\\"opened\\\"\\n          }\\n        ]\\n      }\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"I-0190\\\",\\n      \\\"provider\\\": \\\"local\\\",\\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"memory\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\",\\n      \\\"labels\\\": [\\n        \\\"agent-ready\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"body\\\": \\\"Concurrent lanes can coin identical declaration names \\\\u2014 root goes red only at import join\\\\n\\\\nIncident (2026-07-17, E-v Lane B vs W7-B3): both lanes independently mirrored DegreeBaseFieldInvariance step 4 and coined the SAME names (pointPullbackEquations, pointPullbackUnit, coe_pointPullbackUnit, pointPullbackEquations_presentation_elem_of_eq/_of_ne) in different files (RiemannRoch/DegreeIsoTransport.lean @ 02875571d; RiemannRoch/DegreePullback.lean @ f26b717f0). Each file was green alone; the ROOT failed only when both were imported (environment already contains ...). Repaired by dedup: E-v consumes B-3's arbitrary-f plumbing. Lessons: (1) grep HEAD and sibling in-flight files before coining mirror names; (2) post-commit acceptance should include one full root lake build under the mutex \\\\u2014 per-file lake env lean cannot catch cross-file duplicate declarations; (3) when two same-wave lanes mirror the same model file, the worksheet should pre-assign the shared vocabulary.\\\",\\n      \\\"scope\\\": {\\n        \\\"projects\\\": [\\n          \\\"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild\\\"\\n        ]\\n      },\\n      \\\"audience\\\": \\\"horizon\\\",\\n      \\\"author\\\": \\\"horizon\\\",\\n      \\\"source_ref\\\": null,\\n      \\\"created_at\\\": \\\"2026-07-17T04:06:50.525547+00:00\\\",\\n      \\\"updated_at\\\": \\\"2026-07-17T04:06:50.525560+00:00\\\",\\n      \\\"comments\\\": [],\\n      \\\"metadata\\\": {\\n        \\\"history\\\": [\\n          {\\n            \\\"at\\\": \\\"2026-07-17T04:06:50.842863+00:00\\\",\\n            \\\"actor\\\": \\\"horizon\\\",\\n            \\\"field\\\": \\\"created\\\",\\n            \\\"from\\\": \\\"\\\",\\n            \\\"to\\\": \\\"open\\\",\\n            \\\"note\\\": \\\"opened\\\"\\n          }\\n        ]\\n      }\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"I-0186\\\",\\n      \\\"provider\\\": \\\"local\\\",\\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"memory\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\",\\n      \\\"labels\\\": [\\n        \\\"agent-ready\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"body\\\": \\\"DD-1c (f) hsurj lane \\\\u2014 STAGES 1-2 LANDED + a BLOCKING OBSTRUCTION for stages 3-5 (2026-07-17, Opus hsurj prover). Follow-on to I-0182/I-0179/I-0171/I-0167. New file Picard/DivisorFamilyBackward.lean (root-wired, green 8649 jobs, keystones lean_verify axiom-clean [propext,Classical.choice,Quot.sound]).\\\\n\\\\nLANDED (two committed green stages, the \\\\\\\"eqns\\\\\\\" half of hsurj):\\\\n- Stage 1 (commit 87d787e49): Scheme.LocalEquations.mul_presentation_elem + Scheme.LocalEquations.presentationDivisor_mul. The Weil divisor of the pointwise product d.mul d' is the SUM: presentationDivisor K (d.mul d').presentation = presentationDivisor K d.presentation + presentationDivisor K d'.presentation. Proof: the product presentation's trivializing elem is the product of elems (germ_res_apply + map_mul), and ordZ is a group hom so orders/coeffs add. LocalEquations-level companion of the landed MeromorphicPresentation.presentationDivisor_mul.\\\\n- Stage 2 (commit b2a85c0b6): Scheme.LocalEquations.unitEquations (trivial system, presentationDivisor = 0) + Scheme.LocalEquations.exists_localEquations_presentationDivisor_eq: every EFFECTIVE divisor D (0<=D) is presentationDivisor K E.presentation for an explicit LocalEquations E (a mul-product of tracked point-uniformizer pointEquations, one factor per unit of multiplicity, via stage-1 additivity + presentationDivisor_pointEquations; Finsupp.induction over the support with effectivity propagated). LocalEquations-level companion of exists_presentationDivisor_eq (which only gives a MeromorphicPresentation); effectivity is what keeps it regular (no inverse/pole factors). This gives the anchor equations F.eqns of a family realizing D.\\\\n\\\\nTHE OBSTRUCTION (why stages 3-5 \\\\u2014 the certified support-separated adaptation + divFamOfDivisor \\\\u2014 are NOT MV-free for general D, correcting I-0182/I-0179): The two pinned charts of relCurve are V0 = pi^-1(P1 chart0), V1 = pi^-1(P1 chart1); they OVERLAP, V0 inf V1 = pi^-1(Gm) is a nonempty affine open (AffineTwoCover.pullbackProd; P1 charts overlap on Gm). A DivisorAdaptation structurally covers BOTH charts: FinCoverData.partition0/1 (sum a_j h_j = 1) force V0 <= sup(chart-0 pieces) and V1 <= sup(chart-1 pieces) (FinCoverData.cover0/cover1). So any closed point z in V0 inf V1 lies in some chart-0 piece (inl a) AND some chart-1 piece (inr b). If z in supp(D), then BOTH piece equations vanish at z to order coeffAt_z(D) != 0 \\\\u2014 every adaptation equation refines d and reads D's coefficient at every point of its piece (DivisorAdaptation.coeffAt_eq_toAdd_ordZ_eqn) \\\\u2014 so neither is a unit at z and the overlap ideal (eqn_inl_a, eqn_inr_b) is contained in the maximal ideal m_z != top. Hence ovlColength (inl a)(inr b) is NOT subsingleton, and the support-separation hypothesis hsep of deg_divFamDivisor_of_separated / subsingleton_ovlColength_of_sep is UNSATISFIABLE for any D whose support meets V0 inf V1.\\\\n\\\\nMathematically this is exactly the Cech H0 overlap correction: for z in the overlap, prod_j colength OVERCOUNTS z's local degree (once per chart), so the separated formula finrank W = sum colength gives the WRONG (too-large) degree; the true finrank W = sum colength - overlap correction = the general Mayer-Vietoris (= the hdeg wall). CONCLUSION: hsurj for a GENERAL effective deg-n divisor is NOT free of the general-MV wall \\\\u2014 it needs it precisely for overlap-support divisors, sharing hdeg's obligation. The support-separated backward construction only realizes divisors supported OFF the overlap: supp(D) subset (V0 minus V1) union (V1 minus V0); those DO round-trip MV-free (the off-chart pieces have unit equations, cross-chart overlaps are trivially separated, and within one affine chart finitely many support points can be isolated by basic opens).\\\\n\\\\nREVISED STRATEGY / what remains:\\\\n1. The MV-free hsurj is achievable ONLY for off-overlap divisors. To close it needs: (a) the point-separation-within-one-affine-chart infrastructure (given finitely many closed pts in an affine, a basic-open refinement of d.cover isolating each in a unique piece with the others' pieces avoiding them) \\\\u2014 NEW infra, medium; plus (b) finite-colength + the field-trivial certificate (c3/c4 free, rank via deg_divFamDivisor_of_separated). Stages 1-2 already supply the eqns.\\\\n2. For DD-R's one-sided dictionary (I-0182): still MV-free IFF P-fib's unique effective deg-n divisor D can be arranged/normalized to be supported OFF the chart overlap. If P-fib's D always avoids pi^-1(Gm) (e.g. supported at a fixed rational point at infinity), hsurj-for-D + divFamDivisor_injective (landed) closes it MV-free. Otherwise the field dictionary genuinely needs the general-MV wall for BOTH directions \\\\u2014 recommend the human/DD-R spec confirm P-fib's support location.\\\\n3. The general (all-D) field dictionary equiv divFamFieldEquivOfDegOfSurj needs the general MV (hdeg) regardless \\\\u2014 it is now the sole XL for BOTH hdeg and general hsurj.\\\\n\\\\nagent-ready\\\",\\n      \\\"scope\\\": {\\n        \\\"projects\\\": [\\n          \\\"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild\\\"\\n        ]\\n      },\\n      \\\"audience\\\": \\\"horizon\\\",\\n      \\\"author\\\": \\\"horizon\\\",\\n      \\\"source_ref\\\": null,\\n      \\\"created_at\\\": \\\"2026-07-17T03:29:29.798284+00:00\\\",\\n      \\\"updated_at\\\": \\\"2026-07-17T03:29:29.798295+00:00\\\",\\n      \\\"comments\\\": [],\\n      \\\"metadata\\\": {\\n        \\\"history\\\": [\\n          {\\n            \\\"at\\\": \\\"2026-07-17T03:29:30.210614+00:00\\\",\\n            \\\"actor\\\": \\\"horizon\\\",\\n            \\\"field\\\": \\\"created\\\",\\n            \\\"from\\\": \\\"\\\",\\n            \\\"to\\\": \\\"open\\\",\\n            \\\"note\\\": \\\"opened\\\"\\n          }\\n        ]\\n      }\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"I-0169\\\",\\n      \\\"provider\\\": \\\"local\\\",\\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"memory\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\",\\n      \\\"labels\\\": [\\n        \\\"agent-ready\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"body\\\": \\\"Source-anchor debt: Mumford tangent-space pages not transcribed\\\\n\\\\nThe W5 tangent bricks (Tangent/*.lean) cite Mumford AV II.4 for the tangent-space-of-a-functor / epsilon -> a*epsilon scaling, but the transcribed mumford-abelian-varieties pages are only 0054/0055 (II.4 rigidity) and 0057-0066 (II.5 cohomology and base change) - checked 2026-07-17. The blueprint Tangent chapter therefore anchors on kleiman-picard only (thm:tgtsp read in kleiman-picard-src/kleiman-picard.tex: truncated exponential sequence, mu_a scaling, H1 base-field square - all verified). Next action if a Mumford anchor is wanted: locate the exact pages (likely the II.4 appendix region or the Pic tangent computation) and run page-transcriber (max 5 pages/call), then add mumford-abelian-varieties:page-NNNN to def:truncExpUnit / def:mumford_scaling / thm:h1_truncExp_kernel.\\\",\\n      \\\"scope\\\": {\\n        \\\"projects\\\": [\\n          \\\"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild\\\"\\n        ]\\n      },\\n      \\\"audience\\\": \\\"horizon\\\",\\n      \\\"author\\\": \\\"horizon\\\",\\n      \\\"source_ref\\\": null,\\n      \\\"created_at\\\": \\\"2026-07-17T01:01:25.869114+00:00\\\",\\n      \\\"updated_at\\\": \\\"2026-07-17T01:01:25.869126+00:00\\\",\\n      \\\"comments\\\": [],\\n      \\\"metadata\\\": {\\n        \\\"agent\\\": \\\"blueprint\\\",\\n        \\\"history\\\": [\\n          {\\n            \\\"at\\\": \\\"2026-07-17T01:01:26.171843+00:00\\\",\\n            \\\"actor\\\": \\\"horizon\\\",\\n            \\\"field\\\": \\\"created\\\",\\n            \\\"from\\\": \\\"\\\",\\n            \\\"to\\\": \\\"open\\\",\\n            \\\"note\\\": \\\"opened\\\"\\n          }\\n        ]\\n      }\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"warnings\\\": [\\n    \\\"Inbox has 29 open memory items (recommended maximum 10) \\\\u2014 archive stale, superseded, or no-longer-key memories if this is not intentional.\\\",\\n    \\\"Inbox has 29 open info items (recommended maximum 4)