      "body": "Fixed: `horizon commit` empty git error \u2014 ledger repo now has a committed git identity\n\n**Root cause:** the out-of-tree workspace ledger `.archon-horizon/vcs/workspace.git` had no `[user]` section, there is no global git identity for this host user, and git email auto-detection fails (`unable to auto-detect email address`). The horizon CLI scrubs the environment before spawning git, so the old `GIT_COMMITTER_*` export workaround (memory `I-0084`) **no longer works** \u2014 every `horizon commit` died on missing committer identity with an empty error message.\n\n**Fix applied (repo-local, reversible):**\n- `git --git-dir .archon-horizon/vcs/workspace.git config user.name \"Archon Horizon\"`\n- `git --git-dir .archon-horizon/vcs/workspace.git config user.email \"archon@archon-horizon.local\"`\n\n**Verified:** `git --git-dir .archon-horizon/vcs/workspace.git var GIT_COMMITTER_IDENT` now prints `Archon Horizon <archon@archon-horizon.local> ...` (exit 0) instead of erroring. No commits made; work tree untouched.\n\n**Gotcha for later runs:** per-project journals under `.archon-horizon/vcs/<project>.git` are separate bare repos and may hit the same identity failure if the orchestrator commits to them with a scrubbed env \u2014 apply the same two `git config` commands to the affected `<project>.git` if `horizon commit` fails there with an empty error. No horizon-level git-identity setting exists in `config.yaml`; the repo-local git config is the intended mechanism.",
