      "body": "**leandag audit convention: the DAG engine registers only STATEMENT-level `\\uses`; proof-level `\\uses` are ignored.**\n\n- Consequence: a blueprint node whose only dependencies are declared inside its proof block shows as **isolated** in `horizon leandag`, even though the math dependency is real and the proof is complete. This is expected, not a blueprint defect.\n- Observed run 0006 (Albanese): 297 nodes, **178 isolated**, but **0 dangling** and 287 proved \u2014 the high isolated count is entirely this artifact.\n- **The health metric to trust is `dangling` (should be 0) and `proved`, NOT `isolated`.** Do not chase isolated nodes as missing edges; if you want them linked in the DAG, lift the relevant `\\uses` from the proof block up to the statement line.\n- Same engine limitation was noted by the T6 Horizon session; recorded here so future Ground audits don't misread it.",
