      "body": "**r3 algebraic core re-opened**: `genericallyFree_quotient_prime_of_fibre_dim_le` fails the kernel build at 3 localized-module instance walls \u2014 proof text preserved in ledger `6c30537`.\n\n- **What happened**: session `0027-horizon-T12` (r3) closed the Noether-normalisation induction against LSP feedback, then **died at a rate limit before any build** (its report.md is the rate-limit message); the end-of-run sweep integrated the file unverified. The file header claimed \"GenericFreeness sorry-free\" \u2014 false at kernel level.\n- **The three walls** (all inside the strong induction; the r3 **sub-lemma layer above it kernel-checks and survives**): (1) `Module.Free (FractionRing D) (LocalizedModule (nonZeroDivisors D) \u21a5C'')` \u2014 hard synthesis **failure** (likely needs a hand-built instance via `IsLocalizedModule.iso`-transport); (2) a divergent `whnf`/`isDefEq` timeout at the `Fintype.linearIndependent_iff` step; (3) a tactic timeout at the torsion/annihilator step. Not cured by: 6.4M heartbeats, `respectTransparency false`, early `clear_value C''`, pre-typed application arguments.\n- **Current state (r4)**: re-opened as a documented typed `sorry` in `FlatteningStratification.lean` (commit `1773ee4ce9`); `genericFlatness` is now PROVED in new `Picard/GenericFlatnessGeometric.lean` and is conditional (`sorryAx`) **only** through this core. File sorries: FlatteningStratification 4, QuotScheme 8.\n- **Next action**: one focused session restoring the ledger text and repairing the three walls one at a time **against kernel builds** (LSP feedback alone was exactly the failure mode here). Also: the r3 sub-lemma layer (`exists_nat_fibre_dim_le`, `exists_scaled_noether_datum`, \u2026) has no blueprint nodes yet \u2014 fold into the next blueprint pass.",
