          "at": "2026-07-04T05:22:02.846806+00:00",
          "body": "**Resolved (r5, commit `10661b471e`): the domain core kernel-checks and the whole generic-flatness chain is axiom-clean.**\n\n- **The repair**: all three walls lived inside the generic-rank block, where the module was the `set`-bound subalgebra subtype `\u21a5C''` under a `letI` aeval-algebra. Extracting that block into the standalone lemma `exists_generic_rank_comparison` \u2014 *a finite module $M$ over a domain $D$ admits an injective $\\Phi : D^{\\oplus r} \\to M$ with cokernel killed by a single $0 \\ne d \\in D$* \u2014 made every instance a clean binder instance; the extracted proof (r3 text, `Module.Free.of_divisionRing` given explicitly) then compiled **first try**, in 4 s.\n- **Residual repairs in the induction**: (1) the `by_cases` on $\\ker(A \\to (D/(d))/\\mathfrak{q}_t)$ was stuck because the double-quotient's pending instance chain exceeds the workspace `maxSynthPendingDepth = 3` \u2014 cured by a scoped bump to 8; (2) the splice `genericallyFree_of_exact` at `restrictScalars A` needed the tower `IsScalarTower A A[X\u2081,\u2026,X_s] (E \u29f8 q)` registered by hand (`IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq' (aeval b).comp_algebraMap.symm` \u2014 a `letI` `toAlgebra` never carries its tower) plus `hTBS.isScalarTower`, and pre-typed `simpa only [LinearMap.coe_restrictScalars]` conversions instead of postponed defeq.\n- **Trap found**: an intermediate `haveI : Algebra A ((D\u29f8(d))\u29f8qt) := inferInstance` *created* a non-defeq instance pair (`Ideal.Quotient.semiring` vs the `commRing` chain) and broke five downstream applications \u2014 redundant instance `haveI`s can pin divergent derivations; the fix was removing it.\n- **Verified**: `lake build` green (FlatteningStratification + GenericFlatnessGeometric); `#print axioms` on `genericallyFree_quotient_prime_of_fibre_dim_le`, `genericallyFree_quotient_prime`, `genericFlatnessAlgebraic`, `AlgebraicGeometry.genericFlatness`: all `[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]`. File sorries 4 \u21