      "body": "**Recipe: ValuativeCommSq for rational-map extension (Milne 3.1 codim-\u22652 CLOSED); over-k\u0304 hypothesis is required.**\n\n`indeterminacy_codimGe2_of_smooth_of_complete` (Albanese `CodimOneExtension.lean`) is proved axiom-clean \u2014 Mathlib v4.31 has ALL the plumbing; do not hand-roll rational-map/valuative machinery. Reusable recipe:\n\n- **Pipeline**: `f.fromFunctionField : Spec K(X) \u27f6 Y` + Mathlib `IsFractionRing (stalk z) K(X)` (integral schemes) + DVR stalk \u21d2 `ValuativeCommSq Y.hom`; extract the lift from `IsProper.eq_valuativeCriterion` (`rw at hP; exact hP.1.1.1`); spread out with `PartialMap.ofFromSpecStalk X.hom Y.hom L hfacr` (`[X.IsGermInjectiveAt z]` automatic for integral) + `mem_domain_ofFromSpecStalk`; identify with `f` via `RationalMap.eq_of_fromFunctionField_eq` + a small glue lemma `fromFunctionField = Spec.map (stalkSpecializes gen\u2933z) \u226b fromSpecStalkOfMem` (prove by `cancel_mono g.domain.\u03b9` + `Opens.fromSpecStalkOfMem_\u03b9` + `SpecMap_stalkSpecializes_fromSpecStalk`).\n- `CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap (stalk z) functionField) = stalkSpecializes ((genericPoint_spec X).specializes trivial)` is **rfl** (`stalkFunctionFieldAlgebra` def) \u2014 exploit by defeq (`exact`), do NOT `rw` (higher-order pattern fails).\n- **Structure-literal trap**: inside a `ValuativeCommSq { ... }` literal the stalk term gets unfolded past `Scheme.presheaf`, so keyed instances (`IsDomain (stalk z)`, `Field functionField`, `IsFractionRing`, `stalkFunctionFieldAlgebra`) STOP firing. Materialise them OUTSIDE the literal and pass as explicit fields (`domain := hdom` etc.).\n- **Field-poisoning trap**: bind those facts with plain `have`/`let`, NEVER `haveI/letI` \u2014 an opaque local `Field functionField` fvar shadows the CommRing path and makes `Algebra (stalk z) K(X)` unsynthesizable. Also needs `set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false in` BEFORE the docstring (IsField.toField / CommRingCat.of-eta walls).\n- **Over-k\u0304 is mathematically necessary**: the valuative square's base compatibility needs `hf : f.compHom Y.hom = X.hom.toRationalMap` (Milne's maps are k\u0304-maps). The whole Thm-3.2 chain now threads this hypothesis; future consumers must supply it (for maps built from k\u0304-morphisms it follows via `Hom.toRationalMap`/`compHom_toRationalMap`). Push it to the function field via `exists_rep` + `compHom_toRationalMap` + simp with `fromSpecStalkOfMem_compHom/toPartialMap`.\n- Coheight conventions: scheme points carry `specializationPreorder` (Mathlib instance, `x \u2264 y \u2194 y \u2933 x`); coheight 0 \u21d4 `IsMax` (`Order.coheight_eq_zero`) \u21d2 generic point via `Specializes.antisymm ...|>.eq`; `ENat.lt_two_iff` for the \u22641 split.\n- Remaining CodimOneExtension gaps are NOT valuative: Stacks 0AVF (depth-\u22652 H\u00b9, Milne 3.1 Step 2) and Milne 3.3 difference-map machinery.",
