      "body": "**Recipe: Stacks 00TT at ARBITRARY primes over a perfect field, Serre-free (supersedes the \"00OF is the remaining genuine gap / do not attempt\" guidance \u2014 00OF is no longer needed).**\n\nProven in `Albanese/SmoothPrimeRegularity.lean` (axiom-clean, v4.31 Mathlib suffices). Structure, reusable for similar dimension-theory builds:\n\n- **Lemma A (trdeg\u2013height)**: for prime `P \u2286 k[x_\u03b9]`, `\u2203 d \u2264 trdeg k (k[x_\u03b9]\u29f8P)` with `#\u03b9 \u2264 ht P + d`. Induction via `Finite.induction_empty_option`; one-variable step uses Stacks 00ON `Ideal.height_eq_height_add_of_liesOver_of_hasGoingDown` (+ `Algebra.HasGoingDown.of_flat`, `Module.Flat.of_free`) and splits on the fiber prime in `(R\u29f8p)[X]` (`Ideal.polynomialQuotientEquivQuotientPolynomial`); the `\u2203 d \u2264`-witness form avoids ALL fraction fields and exact-trdeg bookkeeping. Key trdeg API: `trdeg_add_le`, `trdeg_le_of_injective`, `Polynomial.trdeg_of_isDomain` (all root-namespace!).\n- **Lemma C**: `rank \u03a9[K\u2044k] = trdeg k K` for `EssFiniteType` field ext of perfect `k`: `exists_isTranscendenceBasis_and_isSeparable_of_perfectField` (returns a `Finset`!) + `Algebra.FormallyEtale.of_isSeparable` + `tensorKaehlerEquivOfFormallyEtale` + `AlgebraicIndependent.aevalEquivField` + `Basis.ofIsLocalizedModule` over `mvPolynomialBasis`.\n- **Lemma D**: `dim_\u03ba m/m\u00b2 + dim_\u03ba \u03a9[\u03ba\u2044R] = n` generalising iter-199 by dropping `Subsingleton \u03a9[\u03ba/R]`: same `iff_split_injection` retraction + `exact_kerCotangentToTensor_mapBaseChange` + `mapBaseChange_surjective` + rank\u2013nullity. `FormallySmooth k \u03ba` is FREE from the new low-priority instance `Algebra.FormallySmooth.of_perfectField [EssFiniteType k \u03ba]`.\n- Assembly: `finrank Cot \u2264 ht q` by \u2115\u221e cancellation (`ENat.add_le_add_iff_right`, pass `k :=` explicitly), then `IsRegularLocalRing.of_finrank_cotangentSpace_le_ringKrullDim`.\n\n**Traps**: (1) NEVER bridge AlgEquiv/RingEquiv coercion paths with `Iff.rfl`/`rfl` at FUNCTION level (whnf timeout on `renameEquiv`); state helpers with pointwise membership hypotheses (`\u2200 a, a \u2208 P\u2080 \u2194 g a \u2208 P`) instead. (2) `have`-bound equivs are opaque \u2014 use `set ... with` when a later proof must compute through the definition. (3) In `of_equiv` induction branches don't `rename_i` (grabs instances); avoid naming the types. (4) Multi-step `rw` chains on algebraMap-towers can close the goal mid-list and error \u2014 split into per-equation `have`s. (5) `Basis` is now `Module.Basis` (open Module).\n\nDead code note: `stalkMap_flat_of_smooth` (Stage 1) and `exists_algebra_isStandardSmooth_section_stalk_isLocalization_of_smooth` (Stage 3) in `CodimOneExtension.lean` now have NO Lean consumers (the new stalk proof bypasses them); blueprint-pinned leaves \u2014 Ground may prune or keep.",
