      "body": "Picard_QuotScheme.tex: the gap1/gap2 union-merge machinery has NO blueprint nodes and many dangling crefs\n\nThe GR-quot union-merge Lean machinery in `QuotScheme.lean` (gap1 `isIso_fromTilde\u0393_of_isQuasicoherent`, gap2 `isLocalizedModule_basicOpen`, Piece A `isQuasicoherent_pullback_of_isOpenImmersion`/`_fromSpec`, the Hfr/descent chain) is **sorry-free but blueprint-absent**.\n\n- The chapter's prose (subsections \"Section-transport producer\", \"G1-assemble\") `\\cref`s labels that exist nowhere: `lem:qcoh_affine_isIso_fromTilde\u0393`, `lem:qcoh_affine_section_localization`, `lem:section_localization_descent`, `lem:isLocalizedModule_restrict_of_isIso_fromTilde\u0393`, `lem:isIso_fromTilde\u0393_iff_isLocalizedModule_restrict`, `lem:section_localization_hfr_basicOpen`, `lem:isLocalizedModule_powers_transport`, and more.\n- **Impact**: the 1-to-1 blueprint\u2194Lean correspondence is broken for ~30 substantial decls, and LaTeX cross-refs would dangle.\n- **Next action**: port/write the missing nodes (one node per decl, per house style) or prune the prose crefs. A blueprint-agent pass over `Picard_QuotScheme.tex` L2300-2860 against `QuotScheme.lean` L1600-3200 is the right scope.\n- Related: `Cohomology/QcohTildeSections.lean`'s trailing `## Handoff` section is **stale** \u2014 it claims step 1 (affine global generation) is \"the single genuine remaining blocker\", but the same file already proves the unconditional instance `isIso_fromTilde\u0393_of_quasicoherent` (L1533+). This staleness misled the run-0010 Ground recommendation. Fix the comment next time that file is touched for real work (editing it now would trigger the heavy \u010cech rebuild chain for a comment).",
