      "body": "**Subproject merge-back recipe (worked for T1 / Line-Bundle-Comparison-Iso \u2192 AJC; reuse for Albanese / Cech back-merges).**\n\n- **Wholesale lift beats cherry-pick** when the subproject built green on the same toolchain+mathlib rev: replace every diverged shared file with the subproject copy, add the new files, then repair AJC-only consumers. Verify first with a decl-name superset check (regex-extract `def|lemma|...` heads, `comm -23`) and a consumer grep for the decls that moved/disappeared.\n- **Check for cross-module duplicate decl names BEFORE building**: two modules both imported by the root that declare the same fully-qualified name are a fatal clash. In T1, LBC's `TensorObjSubstrate.lean` had absorbed 13 decls of AJC's `PullbackTensorComp.lean` (incl. `pullbackTensorMap_restrict`) \u2192 the right fix was to **retire the superseded module** (its 8 unique helpers had no consumers).\n- **Blueprint: port per-chapter, not per-project.** Wholesale-copy a chapter only after a comment-stripped cross-ref check: (refs of incoming chapter) \u2286 (its labels \u222a other AJC chapters' labels), and no other AJC chapter references a disappearing label. In T1 the TOS chapter ported cleanly; LBC's restructured `RelPicFunctor`/`LineBundlePullback` chapters did NOT (6 `\\cref` sites in `Picard_FGAPicRepresentability.tex` would dangle) \u2014 kept AJC's copies. Their reconciliation is optional future work.\n- Big-file build times on this box: `TensorObjSubstrate.lean` (4592 L) + `TensorObjInverse.lean` (3424 L) + rest of the cone \u2248 15 min wall with warm mathlib cache.",
