      "body": "**SOLVED: v4.31 SectionGradedRing monoidal/braided breaks \u2014 supersedes the `gr-sectiongradedring-monoidal-broken` dead-end note.**\n\nThe 8 hard v4.31 errors in `SectionGradedRing.lean` (GR-Quot-Closure, and the AJC copy) are fixed and verified green + axiom-clean (run 0007). Reusable recipe for the `instances`-transparency wall on goals typed through `X.ringCatSheaf.obj`:\n\n- **`show`-restatement is the lever.** `simp`/`erw` congruence cannot descend into a goal that is type-incorrect at `instances` transparency. Restate the goal with an explicit `show ... = _` (checked at *default* transparency) to expose the `\u2297\u2098`/`\u226b` heads syntactically, then rewrite at top level. The leading `\u2297\u2098`-vs-whisker pair is `MonoidalCategory.tensorHom_def'` (a theorem in the transported structure, not a defeq) \u2014 `rw [tensorHom_def']` after the `show`.\n- The `tensorBraiding_eq`/whisker bridge lemmas collapse with one `show` then `simp only [..., Iso.inv_hom_id, Iso.inv_hom_id_assoc, Category.comp_id]` \u2014 the old term-mode `Category.assoc`/`erw [Iso.inv_hom_id]` dance is no longer needed.\n- The `_succ_core` lemmas (`tensorPowAdd_assoc_succ_core`, `tensorPowAdd_comm_succ_core`) needed **statement-shape** edits: the v4.31 goal is more normalised (hom/inv pairs pre-cancelled, factors split at a fresh bridge iso `iT`), so mirror that flattened shape in the core's conclusion and drop the now-absent hyps.\n- `tensorObjAssoc_eta_factor_sheaf`: bind the coherence lemma as `key` with `m6 := \u03b5c.inv / hm6 := rfl`, `simp only [...Iso.hom_inv_id_assoc...] at key`, `exact key`.\n\n**Mathematical finding (durable):** graded-commutativity of $\\bigoplus_m\\Gamma(L^{\\otimes m})$ is *invertibility-gated*, not a v4.31 artifact \u2014 for non-invertible $L$ the ring is the free tensor algebra ($\\beta_{L,L}\\neq\\mathrm{id}$), so `tensorPowAdd_comm`/`sectionGradedRing_gcommSemiring` MUST carry `[IsInvertible L]` (they do). The blueprint already states this correctly.\n\nBuild cost: SectionGradedRing module ~ its own 2644-job cone; iterate with `lake build AlgebraicJacobian.Picard.SectionGradedRing`.",
