      "body": "**IdentityComponent `isSubgroupHomomorphism` + `baseChangeIso` CLOSED, axiom-clean (run 0005 session 0011, T5).** File sorries 8 \u2192 6; all 6 remaining are blocked (QC\u2227GeomIrred conjunct needs EGA IV\u2082 4.6.1-type input; 5 Pic\u2070 decls FGA-tainted). Recipes:\n\n- **Subgroup object via Yoneda**: `GrpObj.ofRepresentableBy` + a `Subgroup (T \u27f6 G)` presheaf (`{f | Set.range \u21d1f.left \u2286 carrier}`) beats hand-rolling MonObj/GrpObj diagram axioms. Closure under mul: factor `f*g = lift f' g' \u226b ((\u03b9\u2297\u2098\u03b9) \u226b \u03bc)` via `lift_map`, bound range by core lemma `range ((\u03b9\u2297\u2098\u03b9)\u226b\u03bc).left \u2286 carrier` (connected product through e). `Hom.group` is a **scoped instance**: `open scoped MonObj`.\n- **`G\u2070 \u00d7\u2096 G\u2070` connected**: Mathlib `[GeometricallyConnected g] [UniversallyOpen g] [ConnectedSpace X] : ConnectedSpace (pullback f g)` + `(R \u2297 S).left = pullback R.hom S.hom` (rfl). UniversallyOpen-to-Spec-field needs `haveI : Subsingleton \u21a5(Spec (.of k)) := inferInstanceAs (Subsingleton (PrimeSpectrum k))` (sometimes ALSO at the defeq-disguised type `\u21a5(\ud835\udfd9_ (Over (Spec (.of k)))).left`).\n- **grpObjMkPullbackSnd unit compat** (`fst(e_{G_K}) = e_G`): `Over.grpObjMkPullbackSnd_one : one = \u03b5 \u226b (Over.pullback g).map one` IS rw-able against a `letI`-bound instance (must be `letI`, not `haveI` \u2014 GrpObj is data). But **morphism-level rw/assoc in the resulting goal FAILS**: `(Over.pullback \u03c6).obj X` vs `pullback X.hom \u03c6` index mismatch is opaque at instances transparency and `respectTransparency false` does NOT rescue rw or post-rw rfl. Working pattern: **point level** \u2014 calc chain of `rfl` steps redistributing `\u21d1(_ \u226b _).base` applications, `congrArg` for every rewrite (incl. `Subsingleton.elim`), `rw` only inside standalone well-typed subterms (e.g. `pullback.lift_fst` on an explicitly spelled lift, with the lift's w-proof given concretely \u2014 proof irrelevance makes the rfl steps match).\n- **Post-rw auto-rfl failures** on \u21d1-coercion goals (identical-looking sides left unsolved): replace `by rw [h]` with term-mode `congrArg (fun m => \u2026) h`.\n- **baseChangeIso iso assembly**: `IsOpenImmersion.isoOfRangeEq (carrier G_K).\u03b9 (pullback.snd \u03b9 fst) \u226a\u226b pullbackRightPullbackFstIso G.hom \u03c6 \u03b9`; carrier identification `fst\u207b\u00b9(carrier G) = carrier G_K` by clopen (\u2287) + preconnected-range (\u2286) around `IsOpenImmersion.range_pullbackSnd`.\n- `SubProjects/Picard-IdentityComponent` mirror now FURTHER behind AJC (needs re-sync or retirement).",
