      "body": "**AJC build-wall reality (run 0003/0007): `CechSectionIdentificationLegMid1` costs HOURS under load, and racing builds are endemic.**\n\n- `LegMid1` (\"~70 min\" documented) took **5h40m** wall at 100% CPU with box load ~65; its rebuild also cascades: `LegMid2 \u2192 LegTop \u2192 LegAux \u2192 CechSectionIdentification \u2192 CechAugmentedResolution \u2192 CechTermAcyclic \u2192 CechToHigherDirectImage` all rebuild (each 20 min\u20132h+ under load). Budget ~8-12h wall for any change that invalidates the `CechSectionIdentification*` chain; NEVER let its oleans go missing.\n- Before ANY `lake build` in AJC: `pgrep -f 'bin/lean'` + check for other sessions' `lake build` (cwd via `/proc/PID/cwd`). This run had FOUR overlapping builders (two orphaned leans from killed lakes, my rebuild, another session's full build). Orphaned leans (parent lake dead) waste their work \u2014 lake re-runs the job anyway; kill them.\n- A long-running lean of mine was SIGTERM-killed at 3h39m by an external actor (likely another session's cleanup) \u2014 detached builds are not safe from concurrent sessions.\n- `lake env lean` on a file whose import cone has a MISSING olean fails immediately ('object file does not exist') \u2014 iterate by temporarily commenting the blocked import and stubbing the 1-2 facts it supplies, then restore for the final build (worked cleanly for `AffinePushPullEssImage.lean`).\n- Instance-synthesis quirk: in big files, `IsOpenImmersion (pullback.fst g' U.\u03b9)` and even `IsOpenImmersion (Opens.\u03b9 ...)` can FAIL to synthesize inside composite `exact` terms (metavariable/universe timing) though global instances exist \u2014 bind them first with `haveI h := inferInstance` (or a lemma) and pass via `@`-application.",
