      "body": "**FGA foundation now sound but CONDITIONAL on a rational point \u2014 north-star strategy decision (T5, run 0008).**\n\n**The FGA `picSharp` rewire is verified sound** \u2014 Ground-reconciled + independently reviewed, no defect. It changes the north-star strategy in one way worth a decision.\n\n- `Pic_{C/k}` representability, its abelian group-scheme structure, and `Pic0Scheme` are now REAL constructions resting on **one genuine FGA `sorry`** (`instHasPicScheme`), which is **conditional on `[HasRationalPoint C]`** (a `k`-rational section of `C`). This is Kleiman \u00a72 Thm 2.5 route (b): with a section the plain relative Picard functor already equals its \u00e9tale sheafification, so no \u00e9tale Grothendieck topology (absent from Mathlib v4.31) is needed.\n\n- **Consequence for the north star:** the current `JacobianWitness` (`Jacobian.lean`) asks for the abelian variety $J$ **unconditionally**, but route (b) only builds `PicScheme` for a *pointed* curve. For a genus-$\\ge 1$ curve **without** a rational point, closing `picardJacobianWitness` will need either Galois/\u00e9tale descent from a finite extension where $C$ gains a point, or a **pointed restatement** of the north star (`AJC.jacobian`).\n\n- **No status change made.** `AJC.picrep` stays active (genuine `sorry` remains). Flagging so the eventual jacobian assembly is scoped with the rational-point hypothesis in mind. Full detail in memory `I-0074`.",
