      "body": "**A 'failed' T8 session actually delivered a verified win \u2014 and the last GR blocker is now closed.**\n\nRun 0007 T8 Horizon session `0007-horizon-T8` is logged as **failed** with report `Not logged in \u00b7 Please run /login`. But its transcript shows it did **real work** (154k output tokens, $31): it repaired the sole remaining red file in GR-Quot-Closure, `SectionGradedRing.lean` (8 hard v4.31 monoidal-API errors), and ported the fix into AJC. It crashed on an auth error at the very end, *before* verifying \u2014 so it never reported the win.\n\n**Ground verified it this session:**\n- Full `lake build` of GR-Quot-Closure: **EXIT 0, 8566 jobs** \u2014 GR is fully green for the first time since the v4.31 bump (closes long-standing [[I-0001]]/[[I-0006]]).\n- AJC `Picard/SectionGradedRing.lean`: green in isolation, headline decls axiom-clean.\n- Diff reviewed: sound proof engineering, no `sorry`/`admit`; correctly gates graded-commutativity behind `IsInvertible L`.\n\n**Two things to act on:**\n1. **Auth/login is silently failing mid-run and mislabeling real work as `failed`.** This burned $31 here and left a genuine deliverable unreported; ground session `0009-ground` produced nothing (empty dir), likely the same cause. Worth fixing the login before the next run.\n2. **The verified fix is uncommitted.** `horizon commit` fails at the workspace-integration step (empty git error; the MR0555258 lake-manifest still pins mathlib v4.30.0 vs declared v4.31.0 \u2014 a plausible guard trigger). The changes to the two `SectionGradedRing.lean` files sit in the working tree; the end-of-session sweep should capture them, but the AJC tree also holds unverified T2/T5 material, so a clean scoped commit would be safer.\n\nNet: T8's objective (close the v4.31 migration debt) is effectively **met** for the SectionGradedRing lane; only the commit/label bookkeeping is off.",
