      "body": "## Review verdict (run 0006 T6, session 0015-horizon-T6): CONVERGING \u2014 real progress, no defect\n\nIndependent review of the CodimOneExtension / Thm32 rewire. Verdict: **genuine progress**, sound as far as source review + token sweep can establish.\n\n**1. False-statement removal is justified.** `extend_of_codimOneFree_of_smooth` (CodimOneFree \u21d2 extension, *any* complete target) was genuinely false. The `\u2119\u00b2 \u21e2 \u2119\u00b9` projection-from-a-point counterexample is correct: indeterminacy = one codim-2 point (so CodimOneFree holds), yet no regular extension exists. This was a true removal of an unclosable `sorry`, not abandonment of a hard-but-true lemma. Milne 3.1's real content (codim-\u22652 only) is now stated honestly.\n\n**2. New lemmas are real and non-vacuous.**\n- `indeterminacy_codimGe2_of_smooth_of_complete` (~90 LOC): genuine valuative-criterion proof (coheight-0 \u21d2 generic point in domain; coheight-1 \u21d2 DVR stalk + `IsProper.eq_valuativeCriterion` + spread-out via `PartialMap.ofFromSpecStalk`). No circular use of Milne 3.3.\n- `existsUnique_hom_of_indeterminacyLocus_eq_empty`, `hom_ext_of_toRationalMap_eq`, `codimOneFree_of_smooth_of_complete`, `toPartialMap_domain`: all substantive, correctly typed, real proofs.\n\n**3. Chain is logically valid.** Milne 3.3's strengthening (codim-1 witness `z \u2208 indeterminacyLocus f`) is present and load-bearing: `av_indeterminacyLocus_eq_empty` applies `codimGe2` to that `z` to get `2 \u2264 1`, contradiction \u21d2 `Z(f)=\u2205`; then `extend_to_av` extends. Once Milne 3.3 is discharged, `extend_to_av` truly follows.\n\n**4. Sole remaining sorry = Milne 3.3** (`indeterminacy_pure_codim_one_into_grpScheme`, CodimOneExtension.lean:1709). No project-local `axiom`; no `admit`/`native_decide`/`decide`/`proof_wanted`/cheat tokens in the changed files.\n\n**Under-reported bonus (verify at your build):** the session ALSO closed the *second* (harder) sorry in `isRegularLocalRing_stalk_of_smooth` (smooth \u21d2 regular at every prime, prev. a Stacks 00OF gap) via a NEW 768-line untracked file `SmoothPrimeRegularity.lean` (trdeg/height + K\u00e4hler-rank chain to `isRegularLocalRing_of_isLocalization_atPrime_of_isStandardSmooth_of_perfectField`). Imports only Mathlib + StandardSmoothDimension (no cycle), no sorry/axiom. Large load-bearing claim under the DVR chain \u2014 worth an explicit `#print axioms` confirmation once the build settles.\n\n**Heads-up (not a defect):** `extend_to_av` and the three Milne-\u00a7I.3 theorems gained the over-k\u0304 hypothesis `hf/hover : f.compHom Y.hom = X.hom.toRationalMap` (mathematically required, faithful to Milne). Downstream `AlbaneseUP.lean` callers must now thread it \u2014 report's Next already flags this.\n\nNote: could not independently re-run `lake build`/`lean_verify` (a build for MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge, sharing the `AlgebraicJacobian` library, is running \u2014 olean-race risk). Verdict rests on source review + token sweep; report claims full build green + axiom-clean.",
