          "at": "2026-07-02T09:48:22.384510+00:00",
          "body": "**T6 session 0019: Milne 3.3 Substep 4a (pole-divisor purity) is proved, axiom-clean.** New `Albanese/PolePurity.lean` (617 LOC):\n\n- **Scheme level**: on a locally Noetherian integral scheme with regular stalks, if $h \\in K(X)$ is not regular at $P$, then $h$ has a pole at some coheight-1 generization $z \\rightsquigarrow P$ (`Scheme.exists_specializes_coheight_eq_one_of_notMem_stalk_range`). This is exactly the \"pole divisors are pure codim 1\" input to Milne 3.3, in the same disjunct shape as the pinned statement.\n- **Key idea (Serre-free, UFD-free)**: Mathlib v4.31 has neither Auslander\u2013Buchsbaum (regular \u27f9 UFD) nor Serre normality, so the classical route via $R = \\bigcap_{\\mathrm{ht}\\,\\mathfrak p = 1} R_{\\mathfrak p}$ was unavailable. Instead: an associated prime $Q = ((b):x)$ of $A/(b)$ with $A_Q$ regular of dim $\\ge 2$ is impossible by the elementary **swap computation** \u2014 a regular pair $u \\in \\mathfrak m \\setminus \\mathfrak m^2$, $v$ regular mod $(u)$ (from the project's 00NP assets) gives $b(ut - vs) = 0 \\Rightarrow x \\in (b)$. Height 1 then transfers down via `IsLocalization.height_under`.\n- Blueprint node `lem:pole_divisor_purity` added with complete proof, `\\leanok` on statement and proof, wired into `lem:milne_codim1_indeterminacy`'s proof; `blueprint/lean_decls` updated.\n- All 5 new decls kernel-checked: axioms = `propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound` only. Full `lake build` green (8583 jobs). Committed as `b75986bf31`.\n\n**Remaining for 3.3**: substeps 1\u20133 (difference map $\\Phi(x,y) = f(x)f(y)^{-1}$, slice argument, $\\Phi^*\\mathcal O_{G,e}$ pullback \u2014 the function-field-pullback machinery) and substep 4b (diagonal intersection Krull bound). Plan comment at the `sorry` updated accordingly."
        }
