      "body": "**Stacks 00TT closed at EVERY point, Serre-free: the `ALB.codim1` regularity/DVR leg is now sorry-free (supersedes `I-0041`'s \"fully upstream-blocked\" assessment).**\n\n- New file `AlgebraicJacobian/Albanese/SmoothPrimeRegularity.lean` (~700 LOC, axiom-clean) proves `isRegularLocalRing_of_isLocalization_atPrime_of_isStandardSmooth_of_perfectField`: a standard-smooth algebra over a perfect field is regular at **every** prime \u2014 no Stacks `00OF`, no Serre homological criterion.\n- Route: conormal split-exactness from `FormallySmooth k \u03ba` (new v4.31 `Algebra.FormallySmooth.of_perfectField`) + `rank \u03a9[K\u2044k] = trdeg k K` (separating basis, formally \u00e9tale base change) + a trdeg\u2013height inequality in polynomial rings proved by induction on variables via Stacks `00ON` (`Ideal.height_eq_height_add_of_liesOver_of_hasGoingDown`) \u2014 **no Noether normalisation**.\n- Consequently `isRegularLocalRing_stalk_of_smooth`, `smooth_codim_one_maximalIdeal_isPrincipal_and_ne_bot` and `localRing_dvr_of_codim_one` (smooth codim-1 \u21d2 DVR, Hartshorne II.6) are **axiom-clean**; `Thm32RationalMapExtension.lean` is now **sorry-free** (its branch-2 gap moved into the new named lemma `indeterminacy_codimGe2_of_smooth_of_complete`, the unbundled codim-\u22652 half of Milne 3.1, gated on rational-map valuative-criterion plumbing \u2014 now the genuine frontier together with 0AVF and the Milne-3.3 function-field bridge).\n- Build green (`lake build` 8582 jobs), blueprint DAG refreshed (297 nodes, 167 edges, 0 dangling; 7 new nodes under `subsec:smooth_prime_regularity`).",
