      "body": "**Reconcile PASS: T5 (run 0005) closed the Stacks 037Q/04KU descent substrate \u2014 a supposed Mathlib gap turned out project-closable.**\n\nT5 (session 0007) is verified correct and green. Independent build + two read-only audits (blueprint fidelity, diff audit) all PASS.\n\n- **Verified:** `lake build` EXIT=0 (8567 jobs); new `Picard/GeometricallyConnectedSection.lean` is sorry-free and axiom-clean (`geometricallyConnected_of_connectedSpace_of_section` and `Algebra.TensorProduct.isDomain_of_isAlgClosed` both = `propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound`); `IdentityComponent.lean` sorries **9 \u2192 8** (genuine removal, not relocation); blueprint `subsec:connectedness_descent` = 8 new nodes, all 1-to-1 with Lean, `\\uses` correct, DAG 0 dangling.\n- **Planning insight:** the roadmap had logged Stacks 037Q/04KU/04KV as *blocked on absent-from-v4.31 Mathlib*. It was in fact **closable in-project** from first principles (Stacks 05P3 tensor-domain over an algebraically closed field + a clopen-image descent argument) \u2014 **no separability/perfect hypothesis needed**. Logged as a `PIC.idcomp` roadmap comment.\n- **Follow-up (not blocking):** the green mirror `SubProjects/Picard-IdentityComponent` is now BEHIND AJC \u2014 a future session should re-sync `IdentityComponent.lean` + the new module + blueprint chapter (see `I-0042`).\n- **Next reachable AJC work:** `IdentityComponent.baseChangeIso` and `isSubgroupHomomorphism` are now unblocked; the remaining 5 Pic\u2070-specific sorries stay FGA-taint-blocked (`AJC.picrep`).",
