      "body": "T6 session 0015: false Milne-3.1 \"extension\" statement removed; Thm 3.2 chain refactored, now gated ONLY on Milne 3.3. Albanese green.\n\n**Soundness finding.** `extend_of_codimOneFree_of_smooth` (`CodimOneExtension.lean`, sorry) claimed: a codim-1-indeterminacy-free rational map from a nonsingular variety to a **complete** variety extends to a regular morphism. This is **false**: the projection $\\mathbb P^2 \\dashrightarrow \\mathbb P^1$, $[x{:}y{:}z]\\mapsto[x{:}y]$, has indeterminacy exactly one codim-2 point (so is CodimOneFree) but admits no regular extension \u2014 any extension $g$ would force $\\mathrm{Dom}(f)=\\mathbb P^2$ via `PartialMap.le_domain_toRationalMap`. The `sorry` was unclosable; Milne 3.1 asserts only codim-\u22652 indeterminacy, and the everywhere-extension needs the *group-variety* input (Lemma 3.3) to first empty the locus.\n\n**Refactor (all built + axiom-checked, `lake build` green, checkdecls unchanged):**\n\n- NEW proved `existsUnique_hom_of_indeterminacyLocus_eq_empty`: $Z(f)=\\emptyset$ \u21d2 unique regular representative (any reduced source / separated target; via Mathlib's maximal representative `RationalMap.toPartialMap`), + helper `hom_ext_of_toRationalMap_eq` (morphisms with equal rational class are equal) and simp lemma `toPartialMap_domain`. All axiom-clean.\n- NEW proved `codimOneFree_of_smooth_of_complete` (Milne 3.1's CodimOneFree phrasing, no 3.3 dependency) \u2014 also closes hint `I-0059`.\n- Milne 3.3 statement **strengthened**: the codim-1 witness must lie in $Z(f)$ (old form was nearly vacuous and could not force emptiness). Still the chapter's single `sorry`.\n- `Thm32RationalMapExtension.lean`: three `CodimOneFree` helpers replaced by `av_indeterminacyLocus_eq_empty` (3.3 + codim-\u22652 \u21d2 $Z(f)=\\emptyset$); `extend_to_av` = emptiness + extension theorem, sorry-free body, `sorryAx` only via 3.3.\n- Blueprint: `thm:codim_one_extension` restated + repinned (now fully `\\leanok`), new `cor:codim_