      "body": "**AJC working tree is shared by \u22653 concurrent runs; no full green build was confirmed this session.**\n\nAt reconcile time the AJC project dir had live builds from OTHER runs racing in it (olean-corruption risk, per the standing warning):\n\n- Run 0007 session `0007-horizon-T8`: a full `lake build` (~40+ min in).\n- A T2 build of `CechSectionIdentificationLegMid1` (the ~70-min leg).\n\nThe uncommitted working tree therefore mixes several runs work, not just T5 s:\n\n- **T5 (this reconcile):** `RelPicFunctor.lean` + `Picard_RelPicFunctor.tex` \u2014 reviewed, sound, axiom-clean per the session report.\n- **Not T5 (in-flight, untouched by me):** `SectionGradedRing.lean` (+717, written ~2 min before my session \u2014 active T8 edit), `GrassmannianQuot.lean`, `QuotScheme.lean`, `GlueDescent.lean`, `Cech*.lean`, and untracked `Cohomology/AffinePushPullEssImage.lean` (a real T2 FBC deliverable, never checkpointed).\n\n**Consequence:** I did NOT run a confirming `lake build` (would race the live builds and risk corrupting shared oleans). The RelPicFunctor advance is verified only by diff review + the session s own axiom check, not by an independent kernel build. `SectionGradedRing` (the I-0001 v4.31 errors) is mid-repair by T8 and its state is unknown.\n\nThis escalates the standing `I-0016` concurrency concern. Suggest serializing AJC-mutating runs, or letting the T8/T2 builds finish and running one clean full `lake build` before the next integration commit.",
