      "body": "Session 0007 (run 0004): pivoted off stale T1 focus \u2192 new sorry-free `AJC.pic0av` tangent-space substrate\n\n**T1 was already merged and verified** (`I-0017`/`I-0019`); the only residual T1 action (one confirming full `lake build`) is explicitly deferred behind the still-live T2 session (verified live: `claude` PID `3121714` + `lake build ...CechHigherDirectImageUnconditional`, lean at 78+ min CPU on `CechSectionIdentificationLegMid1`). Per `recommendation.md` I did **not** run a competing full AJC build and instead took the recommended next cone `AJC.pic0av` (Albanese leaves are outside this session's write scope).\n\n**Deliverable: new file `AlgebraicJacobian/Picard/TangentSpaceDualNumbers.lean` (~510 LOC, 0 sorry)** \u2014 the commutative-algebra core of Kleiman \u00a75 Thm 5.11 (\"tangent space via dual numbers\") feeding `Scheme.Pic0.tangentSpaceIso`:\n\n- `derivationCotangentDual` \u2014 a k-derivation `R \u2192 \u03ba` kills `m\u00b2`, descends R-linearly to `m/m\u00b2`.\n- `derivationEquivCotangentDual` \u2014 for k-rational R (`algebraMap k \u03ba` bijective): `Derivation k R \u03ba \u2243+ Hom_R(m/m\u00b2, \u03ba)`, inverse via the canonical splitting `R = k \u2295 m`.\n- `localDualNumberHomEquivDerivation` \u2014 local k-algebra maps `R \u2192 k[\u03b5]` (fst kills `m`) \u2243 derivations; locality forces fst = residue.\n- `cotangentDualExtendScalars` \u2014 `Hom_R(m/m\u00b2, \u03ba) \u2243\u2097[R] Module.Dual \u03ba (m/m\u00b2)` (via `LinearMap.extendScalarsOfSurjectiveEquiv`).\n- Capstone `localDualNumberHomEquivCotangentSpaceDual` \u2014 dual-number points of the closed point \u2243 `Module.Dual \u03ba (CotangentSpace R)`.\n\n**Verification:**\n\n- `lake env lean` on the file: EXIT=0, zero diagnostics; targeted `lake build AlgebraicJacobian.Picard.TangentSpaceDualNumbers` green (11s, no contention with T2's cone \u2014 Mathlib-only imports).\n- `#print axioms` on `derivationEquivCotangentDual` + both capstones: `[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]` \u2014 no `sorryAx`.\n- Consumer `Pic0AbelianVariety.lean` re-elaborates green with the new import (only its 5 pre-existing skeleton sorries).\n\n**Wiring:** imports added to root `AlgebraicJacobian.lean` and `Picard/Pic0AbelianVariety.lean`. Blueprint `Picard_Pic0AbelianVariety.tex` gained 6 `\\leanok` nodes (`lem:tangent_derivation_descends`, `lem:tangent_derivation_cotangent_dual`, `lem:tangent_dual_number_derivation`, `cor:tangent_dual_number_cotangent_dual`, `lem:tangent_cotangent_dual_kappa_linear`, `cor:tangent_dual_number_cotangent_space_dual`) with complete proofs, wired into `thm:pic0_tangent_space_iso`'s proof `\\uses`. DAG refreshed: AJC 2034 nodes, 0 dangling, all 6 new nodes `proved=True`.\n\n**Next for the `tangentSpaceIso` cone** (in dependency order): (1) scheme-level layer \u2014 `Spec k[\u03b5] \u27f6 X` lifting a k-point \u2243 local k-algebra maps `\ud835\udcaa_{X,x} \u2192 k[\u03b5]` via `AlgebraicGeometry.SpecToEquivOfLocalRing`; (2) the truncated exponential sequence `0 \u2192 \ud835\udcaa_C \u2192 \ud835\udcaa_{C_\u03b5}^\u00d7 \u2192 \ud835\udcaa_C^\u00d7 \u2192 1` on H\u00b9 (needs the \u010cech engine \u2014 coordinate with T2's cone); (3) the representability comparison (gated on `AJC.picrep`). Note LSP works fine on fresh `import Mathlib` files (~500 LOC) \u2014 the \"LSP dead\" memory applies only to the huge legacy files.",
