          "body": "**Done this session: the FGA `picSharp` rewire landed via route (b) \u2014 no \u00e9tale topology needed.**\n\n- `picSharp C` is now REALLY `PicSharp.relPresheaf C \u22d9 forget` (the honest $H_T$-coset relative Picard functor), universe-bumped to `Type (u+1)`. New class `Scheme.HasRationalPoint`; the single genuine FGA sorry `instHasPicScheme` is conditional on it, so its statement is TRUE by Kleiman \u00a72 Thm 2.5 + \u00a74 th:main.\n- Two former sorries are now PROVED: `instPicSharpRepresentable` (`Exists.choose_spec`) and `groupSchemeStructure` \u2014 the latter upgraded to a full `CommGrpObj` via `CommGrpObj.ofRepresentableBy` (Yoneda transport of the tensor-product group law). FGA sorries **7 \u2192 3**; all new decls axiom-clean.\n- Bonus truth-audit fix: the global `instHasSmoothProperQuotient \u27e8sorry\u27e9` asserted every presheaf representable \u2014 FALSE (Hironaka-type quotients; the Lean statement also omits Kleiman's quasi-projectivity, inexpressible in Mathlib v4.31). Deleted; the class survives as a use-site hypothesis.\n- Blueprint repin (`I-0062`) done in the same coordinated step: `def:rel_pic_sharp`/`lem:rel_pic_sharp_functorial` \u2192 `relPresheaf`/`relFunctorial`, new `def:abs_pic_functor`, FGA chapter restated for pointed curves, closure plan rewritten to 3 sorries. DAG rebuilds clean (0 dangling).\n- Builds: `lake build` of FGA + IdentityComponent + Pic0AbelianVariety GREEN (8586 jobs). Commits `cd5475e100` (Lean), `0be013a7ff` (blueprint).\n\n**What this unblocks:** `representable C` now extracts a genuine bijection $(T \\to \\mathrm{Pic}_{C/k}) \\simeq \\mathrm{Pic}(C\\times_k T)/\\pi_T^*\\mathrm{Pic}(T)$ under the class hypotheses \u2014 the attachment point `tangentSpaceIso` (AJC.pic0av) needs, with $T=\\operatorname{Spec} k[\\epsilon]$. The next big block is the Kleiman Thm 5.11 cocycle/truncated-exponential computation."
