      "body": "Albanese: 6 new SmoothPrimeRegularity blueprint \\lean pins absent from blueprint/lean_decls; one pin is to a private decl\n\nThe run added 7 blueprint nodes with `\\lean{}` pins but none are registered in `blueprint/lean_decls` (a 895-line, namespace-sorted full-project decl dump). Verified missing at working tree:\n\n- `MvPolynomial.exists_le_trdeg_and_natCard_le_height_add`\n- `Algebra.IsStandardSmoothOfRelativeDimension.exists_le_trdeg_and_natCast_le_height_add`\n- `Algebra.rank_kaehlerDifferential_eq_trdeg`\n- `finrank_cotangentSpace_add_finrank_kaehler_residueField`\n- `isRegularLocalRing_of_isLocalization_atPrime_of_isStandardSmooth_of_perfectField`\n- `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.RationalMap.indeterminacy_codimGe2_of_smooth_of_complete`\n\nThe run *did* remove dead decls from `lean_decls` but did not add these public ones, so the file is stale w.r.t. `SmoothPrimeRegularity.lean`. `Algebra.*` decls do belong in this file (one was just removed), so the omission is a real registry gap: leandag/checkdecls will see these blueprint pins as dangling and the new (proved, sorry-free) nodes will not register as proved in the DAG.\n\nSeparately, blueprint node `lem:polynomial_step_height_trdeg` pins `Polynomial.step_height_trdeg_of_isPrime`, which is declared `private` (`SmoothPrimeRegularity.lean:177`) \u2014 not resolvable by fully-qualified name from outside the module.\n\n**Action:** regenerate/refresh `blueprint/lean_decls` to include the 6 public decls, and either make `step_height_trdeg_of_isPrime` non-private or drop its \\lean pin. Not covered by existing `I-0049` (that item reviewed the blueprint prose and predates this state).",
