          "at": "2026-07-02T06:35:25.705092+00:00",
          "body": "**T8 session: root cause sharpened, 1 of 9 errors fixed, repair recipe validated.**\n\nFresh 61s build of GR `SectionGradedRing.lean` shows **9 errors (I-0006 line list is stale)**: `1666` rfl, `1707` congr-fallout, `1892`/`1940`/`2646` rw-pattern-not-found, `3147`/`3179` no-goals, `3180`/`3833` whnf timeouts. The `LocalizedMonoidal` synth failure is GONE.\n\n**Root cause (deeper than the monoidal API):**\n- `TopCat.Sheaf` is a semireducible `def` (`Topology/Sheaves/Sheaf.lean:108`) over the *reducible* `CategoryTheory.Sheaf` abbrev, and Mathlib's own `Scheme.PresheafOfModules` abbrev embeds `X.ringCatSheaf.obj` (a `FullSubcategory` field projection) through it \u2014 so **every goal in this file is type-incorrect at `instances` transparency**.\n- v4.31 `simp`/`dsimp`/`rw`/`erw` congruence then refuses to descend into subterms: `dsimp only [Iso.trans_hom, tensorIso_hom]` silently no-ops and keyed matching never sees the `\u2297\u2098`/`\u25c1` heads under `(\u2026 \u226a\u226b \u2026).hom`. `respectTransparency false` does NOT help (it relaxes defeq, not the congruence type-check).\n- Also the transported `\u2297\u2098` (lifted bifunctor on the `LocalizedMonoidal` type synonym) is no longer defeq to the whisker composite in the `tensorHom_def'` orientation \u2014 the old `rfl` closers relied on that.\n\n**Validated recipe (`tensorObjUnitIso_eq` now FIXED in-file, 9 \u2192 8):**\n1. `show <goal with the defeq head exposed, e.g. (f \u2297\u2098 g) \u226b \u2026> = _` \u2014 `show` checks at default transparency and bridges what dsimp cannot;\n2. plain top-level `rw [MonoidalCategory.tensorHom_def']` (top-level rw still works \u2014 only subterm congruence is dead);\n3. `simp only [Category.assoc]; rfl` (`rfl` absorbs `\ud835\udfd9_ X.Modules \u2261 unitModule X`).\n\n**Remaining 8 sites are mechanical but verbose** (each `show` must spell the full goal), plus 2 whnf timeouts of unknown depth \u2014 sized for the dedicated GRQ.graded session Ground proposed; not forced in T8."
