          "body": "**CLOSED \u2014 `SectionGradedRing.lean` is green; full GR `lake build` succeeds (8566 jobs), axiom-clean.** All 8 remaining v4.31 sites fixed this session (T8, run 0007):\n\n- The three monoidal bridge lemmas (`tensorBraiding_eq`, `tensorObjWhiskerLeftIso_eq`, `tensorObjWhiskerRightIso_eq`) \u2014 identifying the hand-built braiding/whiskerings with the canonical $\\beta$/$\\triangleleft$/$\\triangleright$ transported along `tensorObjIso` \u2014 closed by the validated **show-restatement recipe**: restate the goal with the `\u2297\u2098`/`\u226b` heads exposed (defeq at default transparency), then `rw [\u2190 hnat, h\u03bc-conj]` + one cancellation `simp only` closes each.\n- `tensorObjAssoc_eta_factor_sheaf` (the $\\eta$-factorisation of the associator): v4.31 simp now normalises the goal FURTHER than the generic-$M$ coherence lemma's conclusion (counit telescope pre-cancelled, $L(\\eta)=\\varepsilon^{-1}$ pre-rewritten). Fix: bind the coherence as `have key := \u2026` with `m6 := eR.inv`/`hm6 := rfl`, cancel its telescope by a uniform-instance `simp at key`, then `exact key` bridges the comp-instance diamond as before.\n- `tensorPowAdd_assoc` / `tensorPowAdd_comm` (categorified $L^{\\otimes(m+m')}$ pentagon/hexagon): the two whnf timeouts were **goal-shape drift**, not budget \u2014 v4.31 simp cancels plain `Iso.hom_inv_id` pairs the generic cores' conclusions still carried, so `exact`'s isDefEq fell into the 1.2M-char diamond. Fix: restate the two private generic-$M$ cores' conclusions in the new normal form (flat, pairs cancelled, one whisker-split at the bridge `iT`); their proofs pass unchanged. Also: v4.31 `convert` now splits the `LocalizedMonoidal`/`X.Modules` instance diamond into an explicit type-equality goal \u2014 close it with `rfl` before the `eqToHom_trans` reconciliation.\n\n`#print axioms` on `tensorObjRightUnitor_eq`, `tensorPowAdd_comm`, `sectionGradedRing_gcommSemiring` = `[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]`. 4 build iterations, ~9 min each. `GRQ.graded` deliverable (Stacks 01CV commutative section graded ring) is now fully verified."
