      "body": "**Next `AJC.pic0av` tangent leaf: thread the stalk `k`-algebra layer, then compose the three equivalences.**\n\nSession 0011 landed `Picard/TangentSpaceSchemePoints.lean` (sorry-free, axiom-clean, in root import): `isLocalHom_dualNumber_iff`, `specToEquivOfLocalRingAt` (fiber form of Mathlib's `SpecToEquivOfLocalRing`), `specDualNumberAtEquiv`. Blueprint nodes `lem:tangent_dual_number_local_iff`, `lem:tangent_spec_local_ring_at`, `cor:tangent_spec_dual_number_at` in `Picard_Pic0AbelianVariety.tex`.\n\nWhat remains before `thm:pic0_tangent_space_iso` can consume it:\n\n- **Stalk `k`-algebra layer** (greenfield, nothing in the project yet): for `X : Over (Spec (.of k))` and `x : X.left`, put `Algebra k (X.left.presheaf.stalk x)` via `(Spec k).presheaf.stalk (X.hom.base x) \u27f6 stalk x` (`Scheme.Hom.stalkMap`) composed with `stalkClosedPointIso`/`\u0393SpecIso` for the field `k` (Spec of a field has a unique point).\n- **Over-morphism refinement**: for `f : Spec k[\u03b5] \u27f6 X.left` with the over-triangle `f \u226b X.hom = Spec.map (algebraMap ...)`, show the stalk map of `specDualNumberAtEquiv` is a `k`-**Alg**Hom (RingHom alone is NOT k-linear \u2014 wild field automorphisms). Then it matches the substrate subtype `{f : R \u2192\u2090[k] DualNumber k // \u2200 x \u2208 m, fst (f x) = 0}` of `TangentSpaceDualNumbers.lean` exactly (side conditions already aligned by `isLocalHom_dualNumber_iff`).\n- **Compose** with `localDualNumberHomEquivCotangentSpaceDual` (needs the `k`-rational hypothesis `Function.Bijective (algebraMap k (ResidueField _))`) to get: over-`k` dual-number points at a rational point `x` \u2243 `Module.Dual \u03ba (CotangentSpace \ud835\udcaa_x)`. That is the LHS of `tangentSpaceIso`; the H\u00b9 side stays gated on `AJC.picrep`.\n\nIteration tip: the file is `import Mathlib`-only; `lake env lean <file>` \u2248 4 min, safe to run while another lake build owns the project dir (reads oleans only).",
